nbsp;Hotel&nbsp;Breakfast,&nbsp;Dinner Clock&nbsp;Tower</td></tr><tr><td>06</td><td>12 JUNE</td><td>6 ZIL HAJJ</td><td>MAKKAH</td><td>5&nbsp;Star&nbsp;Hotel&nbsp;Breakfast,&nbsp;Dinner Clock&nbsp;Tower</td></tr><tr><td>07</td><td>13 JUNE</td><td>7 ZIL HAJJ</td><td>MAKKAH</td><td>5<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Star&nbsp;Hotel&nbsp;Breakfast,&nbsp;Dinner Clock&nbsp;Tower</td></tr><tr><td>08</td><td>14 JUNE</td><td>8 ZIL HAJJ</td><td>MINAH</td><td>Minah&nbsp;Camp&nbsp;Full Board Meals</td></tr><tr><td>09</td><td>15 JUNE</td><td>9 ZIL HAJJ</td><td>ARAFAT</td><td>Arafat Tent Lunch Buffet</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>16 JUNE</td><td>10 ZIL HAJJ</td><td>MAKKAH / MINAH</td><td>Makkah Hotel No Meals Till 12 Zil Hajj, Dinner Maktab&nbsp;A&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>17 JUNE</td><td>11 ZIL HAJJ</td><td>MINAH</td><td>Minah Tent Full Board Meals Maktab&nbsp;A&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>18 JUNE</td><td>12 ZIL HAJJ</td><td>MAKKAH</td><td>Makkah Hotel With Dinner Clock&nbsp;Tower</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>19 JUNE</td><td>13 ZIL HAJJ</td><td>MAKKAH</td><td>Makkah Hotel BreakFast &amp; Dinner Clock&nbsp;Tower</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>20 JUNE</td><td>14 ZIL HAJJ</td><td>JEDDAH</td><td>After Breakfast, Transfer To Jeddah Airport(Flight) and Back Home.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Quad Room Per Person</strong></th><th><strong>Triple Room Per Person</strong></th><th><strong>Double Room Per Person</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pound £ 10200</td><td>Pound £ 10980</td><td>Pound £ 12900</td></tr><tr><td>Euro € 11975</td><td>Euro € 12900</td><td>Euro € 15140</td></tr><tr><td>USD $ 12945</td><td>USD $ 13950</td><td>USD $ 16365</td></tr><tr><td>PKR 3832000</td><td>PKR 4129000</td><td>PKR 4844000</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-17 05:29:04','2024-03-27 10:31:47'),(811,14,'Hajj Guide - How to Perform Hajj - Step By Step Guide to Perform Hajj - Rehman Travels','Hajj Guide, how to perform Hajj, step By Step Guide to perform Hajj, completed guide to wear Ihram and to perform the rites of Hajj.','https://www.rehmantravel.com/hajj/hajj-guide','hajj/hajj-guide','Hajj Guide',NULL,NULL,'Hajj','USD','0.00',6,NULL,'','','',0,0,'<h2>How to perform Hajj Step By Step Guide</h2><h4><a href=\"/ckeditor_images/files/hajj-presentation-updated.pps\">Download Hajj Guide</a></h4><p>Being a Muslim, Faith on five pillars of Islam is very important. These five pillars are:</p><ol><li>Shahada (Oneness of ALLAH)</li><li>Salat (Prayers)</li><li>Roza (Fasting)</li><li>Zakat (Charity)</li><li>Hajj ( To make Pilgrimage)</li></ol><p>Hajj is the 5th important pillar of Islam. It is obligatory for every Muslim to perform this annual pilgrimage (HAJJ) to Makkah once in a lifetime if he is physically and financially sound.</p><p>The history of hajj roots to around 2000BC when ALLAH ordered Prophet Ibrahim to leave his wife Hazrat Hajra and son Hazrat Ismail alone in the deserts of Makkah. Where Hazrat Hajra desperately ran between the mountains of Safa and Marwa in search of water for her son. she found nothing, and on her return to Hazrat Ismail, she saw the baby scratching the ground with his feet and water fountain sprang forth underneath his foot. Later Prophet Ibrahim was commanded by ALLAH to build Kaab’ah at this Place and invite people to pilgrimage there.</p><p>From that day Hajj started with number of rituals to be performed from 8th Zil Hajj (the last Islamic Month) to 12th Zil Hajj according to Islamic calender.</p><p>There are three (3) types of Hajj:</p><ol><li>Hajj Tamattu ( performing Umrah and Hajj with a separate Ihram for Each)</li><li>Hajj Qiran (combining umrah and Hajj in same Ihram)</li><li>Hajj Ifrad (only Hajj)</li></ol><p>The people outside from Saudi Arabia Usually perform Hajj Tamattu. The pilgrims wear Ihram for Umrah and perform Umrah first. Then they put on their ordinary dress and on 8th Zil Hajj they put on Ihram for Hajj and perform the rites of Hajj. It (the Ihram) is then taken off on the day of Sacrifice (Qurbani).</p><h2>The Umrah</h2><p>There are four (4) Rites of Umrah:</p><ol><li>Putting up of Ihram</li><li>Tawaf</li><li>Sa’yee</li><li>Qasar / Halaq</li></ol><p><strong>1. Ihram</strong></p><p>A pilgrim sets niyyah (intention) of Hajj &amp; Umrah and recites Talbiya before Meqat.</p><p><strong>Procedures of Ihram</strong></p><ol><li>Take a bath (Ghusal) with the intention of Ihram</li><li>Wear ihram sheets</li><li>Offer two Rakat of Nafal by covering your head.</li><li>With your head uncover declare your intention/ Niyyah :</li></ol><h3>اَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّيْ أُرِيْدُ الْحَجَّ فَيَسْرِهُ لِيْ وَ تَقَبَّلْهُ مِنِّيْ</h3><ol><li><i>“O ALLAH! I intend to perform Hajj, please make it easy for me and accept it from me”</i></li><li>Start reciting Talbiya continuously. It is compulsory to recite Talbiya loudly once.</li><li>Enter Masjid Al Haram: Recite Darud e Sharif and Supplicate to ALLAH and proceed towards Kabah.</li><li>Keep your eyes fixed at Baitullah and Say:</li></ol><h3>اللّهُ أكبر اللّهُ أكبر, لا إلَهَ الا اللّه, اللّهُ أكبر اللّهُ اكبر, و لِلّه الحمدَ</h3><ol><li>After this recite Talbiya and move forward to perform Tawaf.</li></ol><p><strong>Prohibitions of Ihram</strong></p><ol><li>Cutting Nails</li><li>Hair cutting Or removing extra hair from any part of the body.</li><li>Use of any scents on the body or on the robes.</li><li>Stitched Clothing.</li><li>Sandals and flip flops must not be stitched either and should allow the ankle and back of foot to be exposed.</li><li>Covering Face or Head.</li><li>Hunting of animals even of lice.</li><li>Sexual activity</li></ol><p><strong>2. Tawaf</strong></p><p>Upon arriving at the Kaabah, stop reciting the Talbiyyah. You must be in Wudu (ablution). Men to leave their right shoulder bare ONLY during the entire Tawaf, this is called Idtiba’a, after the tawaf men need to cover both shoulders.</p><ol><li>Start at the Black Stone, either</li><li>Kiss it if you can, if not.</li><li>Touch it with your right hand, if not</li><li>Face the Black Stone and point at it with your right hand</li></ol><p>Say</p><h3>بِسْمِ اللَّهِ, اللّهُ أكبر</h3><p>(just before kissing it/or just before or whilst touching/pointing) For men, to Raml (hasten/briskly walk) during the first 3 rounds of Tawaf and walk normally during the other 4 rounds. Once you reach the Yamani corner, either Touch it with your right hand (do not kiss it), and say <strong>بِسْمِ اللَّهِ, اللّهُ أكبر</strong> or if unable, then continue without gesturing or saying anything From the Yamani corner to the Black Stone recite This means moving around Kabah seven times with respect and devotion.The pilgrims must walk keeping Kabah on their left. When they will reach at Rukh al Yamani (the fourth corner of Kabah) they should only touch Hijra e Aswad (the Black stone) and Say</p><h3>رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَ فِي الآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَ قِنَا عَذَابَ النَّار</h3><p><i>“Our Lord grant us good in this life and Hereinafter.”</i><br>At the End of Seven circles they will do Istilam (touch or kiss the Black Stone) and say</p><h3>بِسْمِ اللَّهِ, اللّهُ أكبر</h3><p>. After Tawaf the pilgrims will offer 2 rakat of Nafal close to Maqam-e-Ibrahim without covering their heads.<br><strong>Zamzam</strong><br>The pilgrims will go to zamzam, which is situated in the basement of Haram to drink the water (Zamzam) while standing and saying <strong>“بِسْمِ اللَّهِ”</strong> and (supplicate to ALLAH) :</p><h3>اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ عِلْمَاً نَافِعَاًً وَرِزْقَاً وَاسِعَاًَ وَشِفَاءً مِنْ كُلِّ دَاءٍ</h3><p><i>“O ALLAH! I implore for the beneficial knowledge, vast provisions and cure from every disease.</i>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>3. Sa’ey</strong></p><p>The meaning of Sa’ey is to run/ walk back and forth seven times between the hills of Safah &amp; Marwa which are situated to the North and South of Kabah. The seventh trip will end at Marwa. After this the pilgrim will offer two (2) rakat nafal.</p><p><strong>4. Qasar / Halaq</strong></p><p>After Sa’ey male pilgrims will get their heads completely shaved, females will clip their hair equal to a length of a fingertip.</p><h2>Here Umrah is completed</h2><h2>Day wise Detail of Hajj</h2><h2>8th Zil Hajj First Day of Hajj</h2><p>8thZil Hajj starts after the Maghrib prayer of 7th Zil Hajj. The Pilgrims will make their preparations for Hajj same as they got prepared for Umrah. I.e. they will take bath/ Ghusal, set intention, wear Ihram and declare Talbiya.</p><p><strong>Departure to Mina from Azizia</strong></p><p>On 8th Zil Hajj after Fajr prayers OR after the sunrise the Pilgrims will leave towards Mina from Azizia while reciting</p><h3>اللّهُ أكبر اللّهُ أكبر, لا إلَهَ الا اللّه, اللّهُ أكبر اللّهُ اكبر, و لِلّه الحمدَ</h3><p>. Here they will offer remaining four Prayers (Zuhr, Asar, Maghrib and Isha) and will stay overnight in Mina.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>9th Zil Hajj Second Day of Hajj</h2><p><strong>Departure for Arafat from Mina</strong></p><p>After Fajr prayers in Mina. The pilgrims will proceed to Arafat ground. Here they will offer Zuhrain (Zuhar+Asar).</p><p><strong>Departure for Muzdalifa from Arafat</strong></p><p>After Zuhrain in Arafat, the Pilgrims will move towards Muzdalifa after sunset (decling of Sunset), where they will offer Maghribain (combined prayers of Maghrib &amp; Isha prayers) and stay overnight. During different intervals of night, the pilgrims will collect 49 very small size pebbles for next day.</p><h2>10th Zil Hajj 1st Day of Eid</h2><p>On the first day of Eid, the pilgrims will leave for Mina from Muzdalifa after Fajr Prayers. At Mina they will stone Jamarat ul Kubra and will perform Qurbani. After the ritual of Qurbani male Pilgrims will shave their heads and female will clip their hair as part of the Hajj. Now the pilgrims are free to remove their Ihram and wear their ordinary dresses and can perform Tawaf al Ifada. Two (2) Rakat of Nawafil will be offered near Maqam e Ibrahim.They will drink zamzam after performing Sa’ey i.e. 7 runs between Safwah &amp; Marwah and will stay overnight in Mina.</p><h2>11th Zil Hajj 2nd Day of Eid</h2><p>On second day of Eid, the pilgrims will proceed to Jamarat from Mina after Zuhr prayers. They will stone all the three Jamarats (Jamarat e Sughra, Jamarat e Wusta and Jamarat e Qubra) in sequence from small to large by throwing 7 pebbles each. After completion of this ritual, pilgrims will go back to Mina for night stay.</p><h2>12th Zil Hajj 3rd Day of Eid</h2><p>Last day of Eid will again start by proceeding towards Jamarats from Mina after Zuhar Prayers. 4th day stoning of Jamarat will be completed from small to large. After stoning Pilgrims will leave for Makkah before Sunset. Before leaving Makkah, the pilgrims will perform Tawaf ul Wadda (Goodbye Tawaf). At this stage all the obligatory rituals of Hajj are completed.</p><h2>Pilgrims may go to Madina &amp; Ziarats.</h2><h4><a href=\"/ckeditor_images/files/hajj-presentation-updated.pps\">Download Hajj Guide</a></h4><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Arafaat</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MUQAM E IBRAHIM</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>JAMRAAT</p>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-17 05:29:04','2024-02-24 01:16:33'),(812,14,'Hajj Policy 2020 - Government Announce Hajj Policy 2018 - Rehman Travels','Hajj Policy 2020, government announce Hajj Policy 2020 to provide more facilities and services to pilgrims all over Saudi Arabia.','https://www.rehmantravel.com/hajj/hajj-policy-2018','hajj/hajj-policy-2018','Hajj Policy 2018',NULL,NULL,'Hajj','USD','0.00',7,NULL,'','','',0,0,'<h2>Hajj Policy 2024 by Government of Pakistan</h2><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4><a href=\"/ckeditor_images/files/hajj-presentation-updated.pps\">Download Hajj Guide</a></h4><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MASJID E NABAVI</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MASJID E HARAM</p>',0,163,'agent','2024-02-17 05:29:04','2024-02-27 00:09:26'),(813,11,'Dar Al Tawhid Intercontinental Hotel Makkah - Rehman Travel','Dar al tawhid intercontinental Makkah, Dar al tawhid intercontinental hotel Makkah, Dar al tawhid intercontinental hotel online booking Makkah, Dar al tawhid intercontinental Makkah near haram and find the cheapest accommodation deals on 154 hotels in Mecca from Rehman Travels.','hotels/intercontinental-dar-al-tawid-makkah','hotels/intercontinental-dar-al-tawid-makkah','Intercontinental Dar Al Tawhid','','','Hotels','USD','0.00',2,'','','','',0,1,'<div class=\"ramadan-packages print-hajj-packages\">\n<h1 class=\"title\">Intercontinental Dar Al Tawhid</h1>\n\n<p>The Makkah Dar Al Tawhid was built in 2001 and spans 20 floors with 600 rooms. Located at an hour drive from King Abdul Aziz International Airport, Al Tawhid offers 430 rooms and 152 suites providing the very best in comfort and luxury and there are five types of suites ranging from Junior Suites to VIP Royal Suites.The Makkah Intercontinental interior features ornate ceilings, chandeliers and marble floors. The Makkah Intercontinental has all amenities including restaurants, health centre and kids club, and a professionally equipped conference centre that caters to all business needs. Dar Al Tawhid offers its guests a 5-star experience with air-conditioned rooms and en-suite bathrooms having state of the art luxuries like bathrobe and rain showers, bathtub and complimentary toiletries.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Location:</strong> Intercontinental Dar Al-Tawhid offers a commanding view of the Masjid Haram. The intercontinental Makkah is located strategically to offer one to explore the Kaaba and Abraj Al-Bait Towers which has the biggest clock face and is one of the tallest buildings in the world. Dar Al Tawhid Makkah is just footsteps away from the Al Haram mosque and overlooks the Kaaba. Simply step outside the lobby and you will find yourself in the magnificent marble courtyard of the Holy Mosque.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Lobby:</strong>The Makkah Dar Al Tawhid has 14 elevators which all have wheelchair accessibility and are designed to be near accessible rooms. The public areas at the Dar Al Tawhid Intercontinental including restaurants, public rest rooms including the parking area all have wheelchair accessibility to facilitate the tired and elderly pilgrims during their stay. The lobby at the Makkah Intercontinental has free access to high speed internet. The Al Tawhid Makkah has concierge services available for guests to make their stay comfortable and pleasant.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Fine Dining:</strong> Dar Al Tawhid Intercontinental has 3 restaurants for guest to choose from, offering international cuisine comprising Middle Eastern, Indian and European. The Makkah Intercontinental offers sumptuous and sizzling international cuisine buffets at &ldquo;Al Rehab&rdquo; and &ldquo;Al Tayebat&rdquo; restaurants. The Al Rehab restaurant at Intercontinental Dar Al Tawhid gives the visitor breath taking views of the Holy Kaaba and offers buffet breakfast, lunch and dinner. Al Tawhid Intercontinental has stylish coffee bars namely &ldquo;Al Safa&rdquo; and &ldquo;Zamzam Caf&eacute;&rdquo;. The Intercontinental Mekkah Hotel also offers round the clock private dining through room service.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Room: </strong> The Intercontinental Tawhid rooms are very ornately decorated and equipped with in-room safe, mini bar and LCD TV offering cable channels and Wi-Fi access. The Intercontinental Dar Al-Tawhid Makkah has spacious rooms allowing you to enjoy a direct view of the Holy Mosque. Each room of Dar Al Tawhid has coffee/tea makers, free bottled water, newspapers and refrigerators. The bathrooms at the Makkah Intercontinental come standard with bathrobes, free toiletries and hair dryers.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Car Parking:</strong> Hotel Dar Al Tawhid offers extensive car parking with spaces for 90 cars with 3 spaces for disabled/wheelchair parking</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Fitness / Spa:</strong> The Dar Al Tawhid Intercontinental hotels offer a fully equipped and modern fitness centre which is situated on the 7th Floor. Thekids&rsquo; playing/recreational area where books, toys and electronic games are available for the children is also located on this floor.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Business / Meeting Room:</strong> The Dar Al Tawhid Intercontinental Hotel offers fully equipped business centre located on the 10th Floor for the business travellers who wish to have business meetings.</p>\n</div>\n',1,163,'agent','2024-02-17 05:32:23',NULL),(814,11,'Clock Tower Makkah - Fairmont Clock Tower Hotel - Rehman Travels','Makkah tower hotel, hotels in makkah near haram, makkah tower hotel, 5 star hotels in makkah near haram, fairmont hotel Makkah, meeca clock tower hotels and find the cheapest accommodation deals on 164 hotels in Mecca from Rehman Travels.','hotels/fairmont-clock-tower-makkah','hotels/fairmont-clock-tower-makkah','Fairmont Clock Tower Makkah','','','Hotels','USD','0.00',1,'','','','',0,1,'<div class=\"ramadan-packages print-hajj-packages\">\n<h1 class=\"title\">Fairmont Clock Tower Makkah</h1>\n\n<p>The Fairmont Makkah Clock Royal tower is a 76 storey luxury hotel and is one of the tallest buildings in the world. The Makkah Royal Tower Fairmont has 9 dining restaurants including Indian, Lebanese and Al Dira rooftop restaurant. In addition the hotel offers 24-hour room service menu.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"Clock Tower\" class=\"width-100\" src=\"/ckeditor_images/images/Clock%20Tower1%281%29%281%29.jpg\" /></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>The Makkah Clock Tower Hotel is part of Abraj Al Bait complex which is has 4000 shops offering all range of international brands. The main feature of the Saudi Clock Tower Hotel is the 40-meter (130 foot) clock which is visible from a distance of 17 kilometres. The Fairmont Tower clock has the world largest clock face and the clock changes its colour at different times of the day so that the time is visible to despite harsh sunlight or darkness.The Makkah Clock Tower is fitted with Green and White lights that flash five times a day which is visible as far as 30km away signalling the Muslim call for prayers.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Location:</strong> The Royal Clock Tower Hotel is 2 minutes from the Kaaba which is accessible through separate entrances from the hotel lobby.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Lobby:</strong> The Fairmont Clock Tower Makkah Hotel offers free full buffet breakfast, luggage storage facility, limousine or Town car service, 24-hr room service, safe-deposit box and in-room safe. The Fairmont Makkah Hotel has 32 elevators located in the main lobby. These elevators can accommodate wheelchairs and offer access to private suites and floor lobbies.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Fine Dining:</strong> The Makkah Fairmont offers nine state of the art dining venues. Mazaq Caf&eacute; caters to the delightful coffee and tea with selection of delicious French pastries and snacks, Atyaf is an all-dining restaurant from the Middle East, Asia, North Africa, the Levant and Mediterranean, The Grill offers the finest steak dining in Makkah, Aja is the noodle restaurant serving the Asian freshest noodles, dum sum, soups and fried rice, the Mazedaris your stop for Indian cuisine and tandoori flavour, Lezzetis the high end authentic Ottoman cuisine inspired by the by Silk road food of lamb dumplings, sweet olive desserts and beef stews which are fit for a Sultan, the Al-Dar and Al Diraare there to offer you the flavours of Lebanese cuisine with a vast selection of hot and cold mezzah along with the finest Saudi Arabian cuisine. In addition, the Clock Tower Hotel offers complimentary dining for children less than 5 years at buffet dining while children aged 12 or under pay half price on the buffet and kids menu.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Room:</strong> All rooms at the Fairmont Tower have LCD TV and spacious en-suite bathroom. One gets to view the Holy Kaaba and live in-room Haram audio.All rooms have full bath refreshment centre and high speed internet access. The Clock Tower Fairmont offers two selection of Suites, Junior Suite which are one-bedroom suites having Art Deco style with live in-room Haram audio, coffee machine 42&rdquo; LCD/IP television and high speed internet access. The Signature Suite are one bedroom suites having lavish d&eacute;cor with Haram/Kaaba view.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Fairmont Gold:</strong> Indulge yourself in the experience of Fairmont Gold at the Clock Tower Hotel. The Fairmont Gold Lounge offers a complete private and highly personalized stay where the Fairmont Gold team extends a friendly, sincere welcome ensuring that your every need is met. In the Makkah Clock Royal Tower, the Fairmont Gold rooms and suites have exclusive use of the 2 story Gold Lounge at 28th Floor and Al-Dira restaurant having international food at 29th Floor offering panoramic views, continental breakfast, afternoon tea and evening snacks featuring Amuse-Bouche. You have access to private lounge and private check-in/check-out including personal butler services. After your experience with the Fairmont Gold, you will never want to stay anywhere else. The suites offered are Fairmont Gold Room, Fairmont Gold Executive Suite, Fairmont Gold Diplomatic Suite and Fairmont Signature Gold Suite.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Car Parking:</strong> Guest parking is not available onsite.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Fitness / Spa:</strong> The Makkah Clock Tower Fairmont has a fully equipped fitness centre, Jacuzzi, hot tub, sauna and steam room.At Fairmont Hotel fitness centre you get to treat yourself to state-of-the-art fitness equipment and to relax and restore the skin, body and mind. The Fairmont Makkah offers exclusive male and female health clubs where you can enjoy personalized massage, skincare and body treatments. Fairmont Makkah offers Kids Club Activities for families with children.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Business / Meeting Room:</strong> The Fairmont Tower Hotel offers adaptable function area on two floors which includes fully equipped business centre with secretarial service, meeting rooms, function area and ballroom. The business centre also has videoconferencing facility and the media rooms are equipped with live broadcast capabilities and live translation room.</p>\n</div>\n',1,163,'agent','2024-02-17 05:32:23',NULL),(815,11,'Hotels in Makkah – Hotels in Makkah near Haram - Rehman Travels','Hotels in makkah, hotels in makkah near haram, makkah hotel booking, clock tower makkah, cheap hotels in makkah near haram, hotels near haram sharif Makkah and book 5 star hotels near haram at low rates from Rehman travels.','hotels/hotels-in-makkah-near-haram','hotels/hotels-in-makkah-near-haram','Hotels in Makkah Near Haram','','','Hotels','USD','0.00',3,'','','','',0,1,'<h1 class=\"title\">Hotels in Makkah Near Haram</h1>\n\n<div class=\"ramadan-packages print-hajj-packages\">\n<p>Rehman Travels offers its clients to choose from a number of 5-Star and 4-Star hotels while catering to the needs of the 3-Star and Economy clients.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Benefits of 5-Star hotels offered by Rehman Travels</strong></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li>Within 0-200m distance from the Haram mosque</li>\n	<li>Offering exclusive access from hotel lobby to access the Haram mosque</li>\n	<li>Kaaba sounds in all rooms so one does not miss any prayer timings</li>\n	<li>View of the Haram mosque or the Mekkah city from the rooms</li>\n	<li>Wheelchair access to the hotel lobby, wheelchair access lifts, rooms offering wheelchair access furniture layout</li>\n	<li>Health Spa facilities after a tiring day to relax the aching muscles</li>\n	<li>Childcare facilities so you can peacefully carry out your prayers and rituals</li>\n	<li>In-house restaurants offering world-class cuisines and dishes under one roof<br />\n	&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>5 Star hotels in Mekkah</h3>\n\n<ol>\n	<li>Inter-Continen