>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">08 nights in above-mentioned hotels&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">08 American breakfasts&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Phi phi island tour by big boat with lunch (First class seats) (SIC)&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">James Bond island tour by speed boat with lunch (SIC)&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Coral island tour by speed boat with lunch (SIC)&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Ripley&#39;s Believe It or Not!! (3 Attraction - except Balloon) (PVT &amp; Pick n Drop by Land Cruiser)&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Choa Phraya dinner cruise (SIC)&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Siam park - Entrance Fee with water Park and All Rides + Lunch (PVT)&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">All airport and hotel transfers in private basis&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:09:02','2024-03-12 06:08:26'),(1309,6,'vietnam tours | vietnam tour package | vietnam travel | RGT','vietnam tour packages from Pakistan, places to visit in Vietnam, vietnam trip package, vietnam honeymoon package, visit Vietnam with rehmantravel.com','https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/vietnam-tour','world-tours/vietnam-tour','Vietnam Tour',NULL,'vitanme-2.webp','World Tour','USD','0.00',2,NULL,'','','',0,1,'<h2>Vietnam Tour Packages</h2><p><a href=\"world-tours/vietnam-tour-packages-7days\"><img src=\"/ckeditor_images/images/vietnam.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a></p><h4>\"<a href=\"world-tours/vietnam-tour-packages-7days\">Vietnam 7days 6 nights Package </a>\"</h4><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Vietnam City</h3><p>Vietnam, the land of natural beauty and the easternmost country on the Indochina Peninsula. Vietnam is the 15th most populous country in the world. On the north Vietnam share borders with China. On the west shares borders with Cambodia and Laos. Through the Gulf of Thailand, Vietnam shares a maritime border with Thailand and through the South China Sea with the Philippines, Indonesia, and Malaysia.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Vietnam Culture</h3><p>Vietnam’s culture is sundry and complex. Vietnamese culture represents the history and reflects local traditions. In the north, ancient temples in Vietnam shows Chinese influences and on the south reflects the Hindu origin. Chinese, Buddhism, Russian, and Indian culture is present in Vietnam. They have admired various cultural symbols such as the Vietnamese dragon, and Vietnam’s national father. Vietnamese people also believe in spiritualism.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Vietnam Capital</h3><p>Hanoi, the capital of Vietnam and located in the north of Ho Chi Minh City. Hanoi is the second-largest city in Vietnam. Attractive museums, ancient pagodas, vibrant nightlife, traditional villages, and stunning buildings attract travelers and the center of attraction in Vietnam.</p><p>We provide the best flight deals at low rates. <a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/flights\">Book Hanoi flight online</a> and get cheap rates with the facility of online payment via credit card.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Hanoi Tours</h2><p>Hanoi offer numerous sightseeing places for tourists such as Hoan Kiem Lake, West Lake, One Pillar Pagoda, Hanoi Opera House, Tran Quoc Pagoda, Vietnam Fine Arts Museum, Turtle Tower, National Historical Museum, Truc Bach Lake, Vietnam Women Museum, The Huc Bridge, Lenin Park, Union Park, Thu Le Zoo Hanoi, Quang Ba Flower Market, Times City Aquarium, Rose Park, Huu Tiep Lake, Rising Sun Park, and Khue Van. Take a tour of these places so now book <a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/vietnam-tour-packages-7days\">Vietnam tour package</a>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Places to Visit in Vietnam</h2><p>Vietnam the best place for holidays and offer great places for visitors. Let’s discover some exciting places in Vietnam.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Ho Chi Minh City</h3><p>Ho Chi Minh City (HCMC) aka Saigon and it is located in Southeastern Vietnam. Ho Chi Minh City is the largest city and the financial hub of Vietnam. From classy restaurants to the street food, and from the luxury hotels to the cheap hotels all are available in Ho Chi Minh City. Must try Vietnamese cuisine if you visit Ho Chi Minh City. Tan Son Nhat International Airport, the largest airport in Vietnam is also situated in Ho Chi Minh City. Metro, buses, motorbikes, bicycles, and taxis are mostly used for transportation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Ho Chi Minh City tour</h2><p>Ho Chi Minh City tour is not complete if you forget to visit these places. Independence Palace, War Remnants Museum, Bitexco Financial Tower, Thien Hau Temple, Dam Sen Cultural Park, Museum of Vietnamese History, Tao Dan Park, Dam Sen Water Park, Dai Nam Wonderland, Ho Chi Minh Museum, Monkey Island, Artinus 3D Art Museum, Starlight Bridge, Rin Rin Park, KizCiti, The Big Mountain, Green Noen, and Chau Thoi Pagoda.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Da Nang City</h4><p>Da Nang is the fifth largest city important port city in Vietnam. Da Nang is the educational center and commercial center of Middle Vietnam. Beaches in Da Nang are full stocked with fun-filled activities and best for those who like to soak up in the sun. Serene beaches with crystal clear water, ancient pagodas, and verdant national parks are the best attractions in Da Nang.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Da Nang Vietnam</h4><p>Da Nang is fully stocked with sightseeing places such as The Marble Mountains, Dragon Bridge, Han River Bridge, My Khe Beach, Sun Wheel, Non-Nuoc Beach, Ran Nam O, East Sea Park, Thuan Phuoc Bridge, Phap Lam Pagoda, Ban Co Peak, Dong Dinh Art Museum, Children’s Cultural Houses, Green Lake Danang, Sun World Asia Park, Black Rock Beach, and Dan Hai Chau Village. If you want to visit these places, then book a Vietnam tour package</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Hai Phong City</h4><p>Hai Phong is also known as “The City of Flame Flowers”. Many streets are lined in Hai Phong with flame flower trees. Hai Phong, a port city and the third populous city in Vietnam. Hai Phong is also the commercial and industrial center in Vietnam. Temples, pagodas, museums, and mausoleums are worth visiting in Hai Phong.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Hai Phong Attractions</h3><p>In Hai Phong, you will visit Cat Ba National Park, Cannon Fort, Tam Bac Lake, Elephant Mountain, Hai Phong Museum, Phuong Luu Lake, Chua Hang Kenh, Vuon tre Kim Dong, Nui Voi, Maison Communale De Hang Kenh, and Nguyen Binh KhiemTemple.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:09:02','2024-02-26 21:59:14'),(1310,6,'Vietnam 6NIGHTS AND 7DAYS','Vietnam 6NIGHTS AND 7DAYS','https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/vietnam-tour-packages-7days','world-tours/vietnam-tour-packages-7days','Vietnam 6nights And 7days','','','World Tour','USD','0.00',2,'','','','',0,0,'<div class=\"ramadan-packages print-hajj-packages\">\n<h1 class=\"title\">VIETNAM 6NIGHTS AND 7DAYS</h1>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/ckeditor_images/images/vietnam%282%29.jpg\" style=\"width: 100%;\" /></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#0000CD;\"><strong style=\"text-align: center;\">TOUR ITINERARY</strong></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">PACKAGE COST starting from&nbsp; $789 per person&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><b style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Roboto, RobotoDraft, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify;\"><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">Day 1:HANOI &ndash; ARRIVAL</span></b></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Pick up at Noi Bai airport and transfer to hotel for check-in (after 02:00 PM).</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The rest of the day is at leisure till having dinner at a local restaurant.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Overnight in Hanoi.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><b style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Roboto, RobotoDraft, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify;\"><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">Day 2:&nbsp;HANOI &ndash; HA LONG BAY&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></b></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Breakfast at hotel.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Enjoy a morning city tour to visit some of the city&rsquo;s attractions including the fascinating <strong>Ho Chi Minh mausoleum</strong> (<span style=\"color:#000080;\">closed on Monday &amp; Friday, Quan Thanh pagoda will be replaced</span>), <strong>Ho Chi Minh House on stilt &amp; one pillar pagoda. </strong></span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Visit the temple of Literature,</strong> which is regarded as the first university in Viet Nam.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Having lunch at local restaurant.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">After lunch,. proceed to Ha Long bay, one of Vietnam&rsquo;s greatest natural wonders and was recognized as World&rsquo;s Natural Heritage by UNESCO.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">On the way, stop over at ABC rest stop.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Have dinner at local restaurant.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Overnight at hotel in Ha Long.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><b style=\"font-size: small; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Roboto, RobotoDraft, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; text-align: justify;\"><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">Day 3:&nbsp;HA LONG BAY&ndash;&nbsp;HANOI:&nbsp;<span century=\"\" color:=\"\"> </span>&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></b></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">After enjoying breakfast at hotel, take a cruise on the emerald green waters of <strong>Ha Long</strong> among the 3,000 spectacular limestone islands, visit <strong>grottoes Dau Go &amp; Thien Cung</strong> and pass by floating village.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The cruise ends with a fresh seafood lunch on board.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Back to Hanoi after lunch time. On the way, stop over at Dai Viet rest stop.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Arrive in Hanoi, walk through <strong>Hanoi old quarter,</strong> you will have time for shopping at <strong>Dong Xuan market.</strong></span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Have dinner at local restaurant. Enjoy <strong>the water puppet performance,</strong> a unique and famous traditional performance.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Overnight in Hanoi.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><b style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Roboto, RobotoDraft, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000080;\"><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">Day 4:&nbsp;&nbsp;HANOI &ndash; HO CHI MINH CITY:&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span century=\"\" color:=\"\"> &nbsp;</span></span><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(B/L/D)</span></b></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Have breakfast at the hotel</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Transfer to Noi Bai airport for domestic flight to Ho Chi Minh city.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Pick up at Tan Son Nhat airport and transfer to the city center for city tour of dynamic Ho Chi Minh City, still called Saigon by many locals.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Have lunch at a local restaurant.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Visit <strong>War museum</strong> which primarily contains exhibits relating to the <span style=\"color:#FF0000;\"><u>American</u></span> phase of the<span style=\"color:#FF0000;\"><u> Vietnam War,</u></span> and is a major tourist attraction,<strong> Reunification Palace</strong> which was the workplace of the President of <span style=\"color:#FF0000;\"><u>South Vietnam</u></span> &amp; was then known as Independence Palace.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The final stop is <strong>Ben Thanh market</strong> which is always loaded with varieties of goods, such as consumer goods, cakes and candies, food and foodstuff, and particularly high-quality fruit and vegetables.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Have dinner at a good local restaurant.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Overnight in Ho Chi Minh City.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><b style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Roboto, RobotoDraft, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000080;\"><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">Day 5:&nbsp;HO CHI MINH CITY &ndash; CU CHI TUNNELS:&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span century=\"\" color:=\"\"><span style=\"color:#000080;\"> </span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(B/L/D)</span></b></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Breakfast at the hotel</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Leave Ho Chi Minh for <strong>Cu Chi tunnels.</strong> Here you will have the opportunity to witness how rice paper is made and to explore the amazing labyrinth of tunnels used by the guerrillas during the war. Return to Ho Chi Minh city &amp; then have lunch at a local restaurant.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Visit <strong>Notre Dame Cathedral,</strong> the spiritual and cultural crucible of the French presence in the Orient &amp; the <strong>General Post Office,</strong> the ancient &amp; with French colonial architecture style.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The last stop is <strong>China town.</strong></span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Enjoy dinner at a local restaurant.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Overnight in Ho Chi Minh City.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><b style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Roboto, RobotoDraft, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000080;\"><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">Day 6:</span></span><span century=\"\" color:=\"\"><span style=\"color:#000080;\">&nbsp;HO CHI MINH CITY &ndash; MY THO &ndash; HO CHI MINH CITY:&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"> &nbsp; </span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">&nbsp;(B/<wbr />LD)</span></b></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Breakfast at the hotel</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Take a full day trip to the watery world of the <strong>Mekong Delta</strong>, just some hours by coach from Ho Chi Minh City.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">My Tho is a prosperous town of 175,000 inhabitants in the Mekong Delta. It is famous for its extensive orchards and immense rice fields.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Take a cruise on the Mekong River to visit the islands. Here, you can have the chance to visit a coconut candy workshop &amp; to taste fresh candy- specialty. Enjoy tropical fruits, honey tea &amp; listen to Southern traditional music.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Get on a small boat to discover a natural canal of Ben Tre province.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Take a short walk in the coconut farm to visit a typical house in Mekong Delta.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Back to big boat by rowing boat on a small canal.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Have lunch at the garden restaurant.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Visit <strong>Vinh Trang pagoda.</strong> Back to Ho Chi Minh city. In the evening, enjoy dinner at local restaurant</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Overnight in Ho Chi Minh city.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><b style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Roboto, RobotoDraft, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000080;\"><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">Day 7:&nbsp;HO CHI MINH CITY &ndash; DEPARTURE:</span></span><span style=\"color:0473bb;\"><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">&nbsp;</span></span><span century=\"\" color:=\"\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"> &nbsp; </span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; (B)</span></b></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">After having breakfast at the hotel, free at leisure.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Check-out hotel (before 12:00 PM &ndash; noon time) Transfer to Tan Son Nhat airport for leaving flight.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">End of services.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><b style=\"font-size: small; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Roboto, RobotoDraft, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 128);\"><span century=\"\" color:=\"\">TOUR COST INCLUDE:</span></span></b></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Hotel accommodation based on TWN / DBL / TRP shares with daily breakfast.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Meals as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Transportation.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">English speaking guide.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Entrance fee &amp; boat fee. Mineral water provided:</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">-1 bottle of mineral water (500 ml) per pax on airport pick-up and see-off day</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">-2 bottles of mineral water (500 ml) per pax per tour day</span></p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Services charges, room taxes and baggage handling</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n',0,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:09:02','2024-02-21 01:59:24'),(1311,6,'Turkey Group Tour | Turkey Tour Packages | Turkey Tours ','Turkey tour packages from Pakistan, turkey places to visit, kleopatra beach, blue lagoon trip, princess island tour, bosphorus cruise by rehmantravel.com','https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/turkey-group-package','world-tours/turkey-group-package','Turkey Group Package','','','World Tour','USD','0.00',5,'','','','',0,0,'<div class=\"ramadan-packages print-hajj-packages\">\n<h1 class=\"title\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space: nowrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);\">Istanbul Cappadocia Antalya</span></h1>\n\n<div aria-label=\"\" class=\"keyword-text _ngcontent-cej-88\" clickabletooltiptarget=\"\" style=\"display: inline-flex; justify-content: flex-start; max-width: 100%;\">\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 255); font-size: 16px;\">( 8 DAYS 7 NIGHTS )</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/ckeditor_images/images/turkey-banner.jpg\" style=\"width: 100%;\" /></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 205); font-size: 18px;\">Istanbul Trip&nbsp;</span></h2>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 1</strong> -&nbsp;&nbsp;Arrival Day<br />\nUpon arrival, we will pick you from Istanbul airport and transfer to the hotel.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Istanbul City Tour</span></h2>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 2 -</strong>&nbsp;(Breakfast &amp; Lunch included)<br />\nAfter breakfast, start the Istanbul tour and we will visit amazing landmarks of Istanbul such as Hagia Sophia, Blue Mosque, Grand Bazaar, Topkapi Palace, Little Hagia Sophia, Firuz Aga Mosque, and Tomb of Sultan Ahmet.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Half Day Bosphorus Cruise Tour</span></h3>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 3 &ndash;</strong>&nbsp;Flight to Antalya (Breakfast &amp; Dinner included)<br />\nGuests will be given an option to choose the morning or afternoon option to start the tour. First, we visit the Spice Bazaar and the tour guide properly guides and will give tips on the best stalls and kiosks to visit. Next, we will visit the <a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/istanbul-city-tour-9days\">Bosphorus cruise tour</a> and visit the Dolmabahce Palace, Beylerbeyi Palace, and Rumelihisari.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"white-space: nowrap; font-size: 18px;\">Antalya Waterfall Tour</span></h3>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 4 &ndash;</strong>&nbsp; (Breakfast, Lunch &amp; Dinner included)<br />\nWe will start a day with the Antalya tour. Visit Duden Waterfalls. The waterfalls, formed by the Duden River and located at 12km Northeast of Antalya. We will stop for lunch and then we will drive to the Old City Center of Antalya where you will have free time to explore the Harbour.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Antalya Tour</span></h3>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 5 -</strong>&nbsp;(Breakfast &amp; Dinner included)<br />\nEnjoy a free day at Antalya. Explore Antalya, enjoy shopping and do what you want to do.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Antalya to Cappadocia</span></h3>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 6 -</strong>&nbsp; (Breakfast &amp; Dinner included)<br />\nAfter breakfast, we depart to the airport for our domestic flight to Kayseri. Arrive and transfer to Cappadocia Hotel. Enjoy the free day for leisure in Cappadocia.</span><br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">North Cappadocia Tour </span></h3>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 7 &ndash;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;(Breakfast, Lunch &amp; Dinner included)<br />\nDay start with the tour of Dervent Valley. Visit the famous place of Cappadocia which is Fairy Chimneys. After lunch, we will visit the famous Goreme Open Air Museum and Goreme Valley.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Istanbul Tour</span></h3>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 8 &ndash;</strong>&nbsp;(Breakfast included)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">After breakfast, we will depart to the airport for our domestic flight to Istanbul and then back home.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#0000CD;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Package Includes:</span></span></p>\n</div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 16px; text-align: justify;\">&bull;</span><span style=\"font-size: 16px; text-align: justify; white-space: pre;\"> </span><span style=\"font-size: 16px; text-align: justify;\">Arrival airport transfer from Istanbul NEW AIRPORT airport (PRIVATE)</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Domestic flight ticket from İstanbul to Antalya to Cappadocia and back to İstanbul&nbsp;</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>2 nights&rsquo; hotel in Istanbul</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>3 nights&rsquo; hotel in Antalya</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>2 nights&rsquo; hotel in Cappadocia</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>7 open buffet breakfasts</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>5 local dinners at hotels&nbsp;</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>3 local lunches during the tours</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Half Day Istanbul Bosphorus Cruise Tour (SIC)</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Full Day Istanbul city tour (SIC)</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Full Day Antalya city tour (SIC)</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Full Day Cappadocia city tour (SIC)</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>All entrance fees mentioned in the itinerary</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Transportation in a fully air-conditioned, non - smoking coach</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Professional English - speaking tour guides</span></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"fo