 style=\"font-size:16px;\">4 to 5 working days required</span></p>\n	</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">la villa suites doha</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Family Suite, 1 Bedroom</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">USD: 95 Per night per rroom&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">For further concerns and queries feel free to contact us.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Disclaimer:</span></p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">\n	<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Quotation Only</span></p>\n	</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">\n	<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">No room booked at this stage</span></p>\n	</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">\n	<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The rates quoted above are a price guide only</span></p>\n	</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">\n	<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Rates &amp; Availability may change without prior notice at the time of definite booking</span></p>\n	</li>\n</ol>\n',0,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:09:02','2024-02-21 01:59:24'),(1328,6,'baku group tours | azerbaijan tour packages | baku tour','group tours, azerbaijan tours, azerbaijan tour package from Pakistan, azerbaijan attractions, baku city tour package, group tour packages by rehmantravel.com','https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/azerbaijan-group-tour','world-tours/azerbaijan-group-tour','Azerbaijan Group Tour','','','World Tour','USD','0.00',5,'','','','',0,0,'<h1 class=\"Title\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\">Azerbaijan Group Tour</span></span></h1>\n\n<p class=\"Title\"><a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/azerbaijan-group-tour\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"width-100\" src=\"/ckeditor_images/images/Azerbaijan%20group%20package-%20Rehman%20Travels.jpg\" style=\"width: 100%;\" /></a></p>\n\n<div class=\"ramadan-packages print-hajj-packages\">\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">PROGRAM OF TOUR:&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<h2><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\">Baku Tour</span></span></h2>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Welcome to Azerbaijan! Meeting our representative at the Baku Heydar Aliyev International Airport and transfer to the hotel. Leisure time after transferring to our hotel and settling into the hotel. You participate in the panoramic tour of Baku city to explore Baku, to be held in the evening and visit luxurious shopping centers. Then you are transferred to the hotel.&nbsp;</span></div>\n\n<h2><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\">Baku City Tour</span></span></h2>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">After breakfast at the hotel, be ready in the hotel lobby by 09:30am from where your guide will take you on a city tour of Baku. Your first destination will be the Highland Park that offers a 360˚ panoramic view of the Baku city, which resembles a massive amphitheater that gently slopes down to the adjoining Caspian Sea! After we depart for Baku Old City Tour. The excursion tour begins with a visit to the Old Town - &#39;Icheri Sheher&#39;. The old city is the heart of Baku. We will be visiting several dozens of historically architectural monuments located in the territory of Old Town, including Palace of Shirvanshahs, the Maiden Tower, several caravan-palaces, mosques, baths, etc. Visit to Maiden Tower - &lsquo;Baku&rsquo;s symbol&rsquo;. Known locally as Giz Galasi, was built in the 12th century as part of the walled city. &lsquo;Baku&rsquo;s medieval cultural spot &ndash; &lsquo;Caravanserai, to name a few. Shirvanshahs` Palace, the biggest monument of the Shirvan- Absheron branch of the Azerbaijan architecture. You can spend a pleasant time in the restaurants that you can taste dishes from national Azerbaijan cuisine. After lunch we will be passing by Baku Boulevard, one of the favorite retreat centers for tourists and inhabitants. By bus you will see historical milestones namely; Baku Promenade, National Carpets Museum - whose very building resembles a folded carpet, House of the Government, Governor&rsquo;s Garden, Magomayev Philharmonic Theatre, etc. afterwards proceed to Cultural Center Complex - Heydar Aliyev Center that is comprised of an exhibition halls, museum and auditorium. Its architecture is remarkable as no angles can be seen in its interior as well as exterior. After dinner transfer to the hotel. Overnight stay in the hotel.&nbsp;</span></div>\n\n<h3><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Absheron Peninsula, Gobustan, Mud Volcano and Shopping Tour</span></span></h3>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">At 08:30 am, refresh yourselves and be ready. Our professional guide will come to pick you from your place of stay and then by 09:00 am, your Baku holidays begin. You will start your journey to Ateshgah for Temple visit. This temple - well known for fire worshippers and fire adorations - is located in the Surakhany village and is called as the &lsquo;Temple of eternal fire&rsquo;. Comprised of Alter and guest cell room this shrine holds the remnants of Zoroastrianism and Hinduism. It is said that the fire holes of this temple forms natural burning fire that lit up natural gas. The guest room cells of the chapel are now reconstructed as a Museum for the tourists. After the temple visit, by around 11:00 hours, you will start off for Mehemmedli village visit. From the village you will proceed to Yanardag Fire Mountain which lies next to the village. Glowing continuously for several thousand years by means of natural gas, this mountain is one of its kind and a true nature&rsquo;s wonder. After lunch, we move for Gobustan which is located 70 km away from the city. On the way you will stop-off at the Gobustan Museum. Though this hi-tech museum is constructed lately it houses weapons, tools, and bones of primitive people, and hence it&rsquo;s an attractive place for people who love history. Then proceed to the UNESCO world heritage site, Gobustan Rock Art Cultural Landscape which has got more than 6000 rock engravings from Ice Age, to Middle Ages. These rock carvings illustrate the routine, culture and lifestyle of ancient men. Apart from all these, you will also find the leftovers of occupied caves, reimbursements and entombments. Gobustan Rock Art Cultural Landscape is the hill and mountain site occupying the southeast end of the greater Caucasus Mountain ridge in Azerbaijan&rsquo;s Reserves shelters more than 6000 engraved images of prehistoric lifestyles, some dating back 40,000 years old. The area is also famous for its natural mud volcanoes there are almost 300 mud volcanoes all over Azerbaijan it is the highest rate in the world. During this trip you will get the chance to see these amazing active Volcanoes&rsquo; from a close distance. After excursions, half day is yours. Make the day memorable with street walk in Baku and you can make local purchasing. And it is your opportunity to Feel the city with local peoples. Make the day happy&hellip; In the evening hours our guide will organize Baku Boulevard with Cruise Tour (depending on weather) and Ferris Wheel Ride (depending on weather). Overnight in Baku.</span></div>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Departure from Baku</span></h4>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">After breakfast check out from the hotel. We are transferred to the airport. We see our guests off at the airport and the end of Tour! We hope you have a memorable time in Azerbaijan / Baku and we look forward to seeing you in the future. Have a safe trip back home and thank you for choosing us.</span></div>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\">TOUR NET COSTS&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Per person in Single room 235 USD</span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Per person in Double / Twin room 235 USD</span></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Hotel to be used</span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Baku : Cross Way Hotel (3 star)</span></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">TOUR NET COSTS&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Per person in Single room 275 USD</span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Per person in Double / Twin room 250 USD</span></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Hotel to be used</span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Baku: Royal Garden Hotel (4 star)</span></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">SERVICES INCLUDED IN THE PRICE:</span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&nbsp;Airport &ndash; Hotel &ndash; Airport&rdquo; transfer by Mercedes Sprinter&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">03 nights of total stay, including 03 nights in Baku, Bed and breakfast</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Accommodation Single and Twin room with Breakfast</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">All day Transfer with comfortable transport in Mercedes Sprinter (04 days)&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Entrance fee for Shirvanshahs&rsquo; Palace</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Entrance fee for Heydar Aliyev Center</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Entrance fee for Carpet Museum&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Entrance fee for Maiden Tower</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Entrance fee for &ldquo;Ateshgah&rdquo; Fire Temple</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Entrance fee for &ldquo;Yanardag&rdquo; Fire Mountain</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Entrance fee for Gobustan Museum Complex</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Mud Volcano Tour by Off &ndash; Road Cars</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Entrance fee for Evening Boat</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Entrance fee for Ferris Wheel</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">01 Drinking Bottle of water per person per day</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">All tours and transfers which are mentioned in the program</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Professional Guide service in English excursions throughout the tour&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Tourism Visa to Azerbaijan</span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">SERVICES NOT INCLUDED IN THE PRICE:</span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Air Fare&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Lunches and Dinners</span></li>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Insurance&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Any others expenses which are not mentioned at the included section</span></p>\n\n<h2><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Azerbaijan Visa Requirements</span></h2>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Passport Scan copy&nbsp;</span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>CNIC Scan Copy.</span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>01 Photos Scan Copy Any Background.</span></div>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Please Note:</span></span></p>\n\n<d