style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Leave the hotel after breakfast and start the day with the tour of the amazing place Red Square.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Then visit the Alexander Garden, Lenin Tomb, Zaryadye Park, and GUM department store.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>After lunch, continue the tour and visit the Kremlin Grounds.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Back to the hotel.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h2><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">St Petersburg sightseeing&nbsp;</span></span></h2>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Day 3:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Breakfast in the hotel.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Visit the Christ the Saviour, famous Verobyovy gory observation deck, the highest spot of Moscow Poklonnaya Gora, Moscow Triumphal gate, Tverskoi Boulevard, Pushkinskaya Square, and the radial street in Moscow Tverskaya Street.&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Lunch at the restaurant and then transfer to the hotel.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h2><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Moscow travel</span></span></h2>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Day 4:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>After breakfast, transfer to the Leningradsky Railway Station and travel to Saint Petersburg.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span> Arrive at Saint Petersburg and transfer to the hotel.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h2><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Peter and Paul Fortress Tour</span></span></h2>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Day 5:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>After breakfast, the tour guide gives orientation about the city tour and you will see Nevsky Avenue, Palace Square, Saint Petersburg State University, Stroganov Palace, Bronze Horseman, and Summer Garden.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>After lunch, visit Peter and Paul Fortress.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Dinner and back to the hotel.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<div aria-label=\"\" class=\"keyword-text _ngcontent-buf-87\" clickabletooltiptarget=\"\" style=\"display: inline-flex; justify-content: flex-start; max-width: 100%;\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span aria-hidden=\"false\" class=\"keyword _ngcontent-buf-87\" style=\"overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\">Catherine the great palace</span></span></span></h3>\n</div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Day 6:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Breakfast in the hotel.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </spa