">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Breakfast at hotel, free day for shopping &amp; leisure. You can also suggest to us which place you want to explore in free time.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>After all the day fun overnight in Bangkok.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Good Bye Bangkok</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 255); font-size: 18px;\">Day 16:&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>After breakfast, we will depart to Bangkok airport for your flight to your country. We hope you had a memorable time during your stay. Have a safe flight back!</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">** End of services **</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">PRICE INCLUDED&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space: pre;\"> </span>05 nights&rsquo; accommodation with Breakfast in Phuket&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>05 nights&rsquo; accommodation with Breakfast in Pattaya&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>05 nights&rsquo; accommodation with Breakfast in Bangkok&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Private Transfer from Phuket airport to hotel in Phuket without Guide&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Private Transfer from hotel in Phuket to Phuket airport without Guide&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Private Transfer from Suvarnabhumi airport or DMK airport to hotel in without Guide&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Private Transfer from hotel in Pattaya to the hotel in Bangkok without Guide&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Private Transfer from hotel in Bangkok to Suvarnabhumi airport or DMK airport&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>SIC Full day Phi Phi Island tour by big boat with lunch (Exclude national park fee THB 400 per person pay on spot)&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>SIC Half day Coral Island tour with Indian lunch&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Private Believe it or not (3 attractions)&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Private transfer to a Dinner cruise on Chaopraya river&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Private Siam Park city with lunch (Include 1 English speaking guide (Some Riding is still closing temporary)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Private Half-day Bangkok city and temples tour (include Marble temple and Golden temple)&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\">PRICE EXCLUDED&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&middot; Services not mentioned in the itinerary&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&middot; All drinks during meal&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&middot; All airfares</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. visa</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&middot; Expenses of the personal kind; tips for local staff in the service industry.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&middot; Items of a personal nature such as phone calls, pay movies, room services, mini bars laundries or&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">other expenditures during the tour.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&middot; Public Holiday surcharge</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">TERMS &amp; CONDITIONS&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Please note that NO services have been reserved at this stage, the confirmation is subject to room availability upon the first-come-first-served basis.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>The booking must proceed under Guaranteed only, full cancellation charges are applicable in the event of any amendment/cancellation charge.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Our proposal is quoted in USD inclusive of GST tax and Net to you.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</div>\n',0,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:09:03','2024-02-21 01:59:24'),(1366,6,'Land Package Combo | Pattaya | Bangkok','Land Package Combo Pattaya Bangkok, Low Cost Package, Pattaya Package, Combo Package, Bangkok Package','https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/land-package-combo-pattaya-bangkok','world-tours/land-package-combo-pattaya-bangkok','Land Package Combo Pattaya Bangkok','','','World Tour','USD','0.00',3,'','','','',0,0,'<h1 class=\"title\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\">Land <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms,cursive;\">Package</span> Combo Pattaya Bangkok</span></h1>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/ckeditor_images/images/Pattaya%20Bangkok%20Tours.jpeg\" style=\"width: 100%;\" /></span></p>\n',0,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:09:03','2024-02-21 01:59:24'),(1367,6,'4 DAY SPECIAL ISTANBUL CITY TOUR | Turkey Tours','Topkapi Palace, SultanAhmet Imperial Mosque, Hippodrome, Grand Covered Bazaar, Bosphorus Cruise, Spice Bazaar, Princes\' Islands, Miniaturk Museum','https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/4-day-special-istanbul-city-tour','world-tours/4-day-special-istanbul-city-tour','4 Day Special Istanbul City Tour','','','World Tour','USD','0.00',9,'','','','',0,0,'<h1 class=\"title\">4 DAY SPECIAL ISTANBUL CITY TOUR</h1>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/ckeditor_images/images/4%20Days%20Istanbul%20City%20Tour.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\" /></p>\n\n<h2><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\">4-DAY SPECIAL ISTANBUL CITY TOUR ITINERARY:&nbsp;</span></span></h2>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 1:</strong>&nbsp;Istanbul - Arrival Day&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height: 2.0;\">Welcome to Turkey Istanbul Airport. Meet and Greet at Istanbul Airport and transfer to your hotel, Transfer from the airport &amp; check in to your hotel. Overnight in Istanbul.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 2:</strong> Istanbul City Tour</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">(Very rich continental open buffet Breakfast included)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height: 2.0;\">After breakfast, we have Istanbul City Tour. Our first visit will be to HIPPODROME. Ancient Hippodrome was the scene of chariot races, with three monuments; the Obelisk of Theodosius, the bronze Serpentine Column and the Column of Constantine. Then we will visit SULTANAHMET IMPERIAL MOSQUE. Across from Hagia Sophia Grand Mosque, it was built in the 16th century by the architect Mehmet and is known as the BLUE MOSQUE because of its magnificent interior decoration of blue Iznik tiles. Our next visit will be to HAGIA SOPHIA GRAND MOSQUE. The Hagia Sophia Grand Mosque, previously known as the Church of Divine Wisdom, is simply the best of its kind! Hagia Sophia Grand Mosque is the greatest surviving example of Byzantine Architecture. For 1000 years, it was once the largest church in the world, decorated with stunning 6th-century golden mosaics. Today it is a mosque. Lunch break at 13:00 pm. After lunch, Murtis Tour will take you to the ASIL EFENDI which is a unique atmosphere with reasonable prices for your shopping. Here you will find; Exotic Spices and Herbs, Turkish Baklava, Turkish Delights, Turkish Coffee, nuts and fruits, small souvenirs such as Ceramic Handicrafts, Evil Eyes totems, all-natural olive oil, soaps, and many other goods in Souvenir Shops and stores. After the tour, transfer back to your hotel. After the tour returns back to your hotel. Overnight in Istanbul. </span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\"><strong>Note:</strong> Please do not forget to carry a Scarf with you because of visiting to Blue Mosque &amp; Hagia Sophia Mosque. &nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 3:</strong> Istanbul Bosphorus Cruise and Shopping Tour</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">(Very rich continental open buffet Breakfast included)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px; line-height: 2.0;\">Pick up at 08:30 from the hotel and depart for the Istanbul Bosphorus Cruise and Shopping Tour. BOSPHORUS BY BOAT is a traditional excursion by boat along the waterway separating Europe and Asia. The shore is lined with old wooden villas, palaces of marble, fortresses, and small fishing villages. During the excursion, you will see the magnificent sights of the following attractions from your boat. See Dolmabahce Palace, and further along, the parks and imperial pavilions of Yildiz Palace. On the coastal edge of this park, is Ciragan Palace, 300 meters of its marble facade faces the shore. At Ortakoy a great variety of artists gather every Sunday to display their work along the street. Ortakoy is a symbol of tolerance with a church, a mosque, and a synagogue existing side by side for centuries. RUMELI FORTRESS Built by Mehmet the Conqueror in 1452 prior to the conquest of Istanbul was completed in only four months to control and protect the infamous Bosphorus passage. It is one of the most beautiful works of military architecture anywhere in the world. BEYLERBEYI PALAS (PALACE) The summer residence of Ottoman sultans exists in its original renovated glory featuring original antique furniture and magnificent gardens with the Harem on the Asian side of Istanbul. BOSPHORUS BRIDGE enjoys a unique chance to step from one continent (Asia) to another (Europe) CAMLICA HILL is the highest point in Istanbul. At the top of it you can rest and admire the magnificent panorama of Istanbul and the Bosphorus from the beautiful gardens, landscaped in traditional Turkish Ottoman style. SHOPPING TOUR (after the cruise) Experience the traditional silk weaving skills of Turkish women at the carpet weaving courses provided by The Ministry of National Education. You will get the opportunity to see jewelry, a handcrafts center, and a modern leatherwear show. Enjoy the experience of shopping whilst gaining the knowledge of the ancient craftsmen, with Murti&#39;s Tour&#39;s local escort full of knowledge about how to haggle the streets of Istanbul. The rest of the evening is yours to explore Istanbul. Overnight in Istanbul. &nbsp;</span><br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Day 4:</strong> Istanbul - End of Tour</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">(Very rich continental open buffet Breakfast included)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height: 2.0;\">After breakfast, check out from the hotel. We hope your tour was a memorable one and we look forward to seeing you in the future on another TravelShop Turkey Tour. Have a safe trip back home and thanks for choosing TravelShop Turkey. &nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\">4 DAY SPECIAL ISTANBUL CITY TOUR INCLUDES:</span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Arrival airport transfer from Istanbul Airport</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">3 nights&rsquo; hotel accommodation at The Central Palace Hotel in Istanbul</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">3 open buffet very rich continental breakfasts</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Guided Istanbul City Tour</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Guided Istanbul Bosphorus Cruise and Shopping Tour</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">All entrance fees mentioned in the itinerary</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Transportation in a fully air-conditioned, non-smoking coach</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Professional English-speaking tour guides</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Return transfer to Istanbul Airport</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#FF0000;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; text-align: justify;\">Note:&nbsp;</strong></span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; text-align: justify;\">Hagia Sophia is closed on Mondays, Topkapi Palace is closed on Tuesdays, and Grand Bazaar is closed on Sundays. If your tour is on one of these days, we would offer you to visit Underground Cistern instead of Hagia Sophia and Topkapi palace museum, instead of Grand Baazar, you will visit Spice Bazaar.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<table align=\"center\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:100%;text-align: center;\">\n	<tbody>\n		<tr style=\"background-color:blue; color:white; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">\n			<th colspan=\"12\" style=\"text-align: center;\">4 DAYS SPECIAL ISTANBUL TOUR PRICES IN EURO</th>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<th scope=\"row\" style=\"background-color:yellow; color:black; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">Per Person In</th>\n			<td style=\"background-color:yellow; color:black; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">TRIPLE ROOM</td>\n			<td style=\"background-color:yellow; color:black; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">DOUBLE ROOM</td>\n			<td style=\"background-color:yellow; color:black; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">SINGLE ROOM</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<th scope=\"row\" style=\"background-color:yellow; color:black; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">Min. 4 Pax</th>\n			<td>&euro; 479,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 499,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 675,00</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<th scope=\"row\" style=\"background-color:yellow; color:black; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">Min. 10 Pax</th>\n			<td>&euro; 399,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 419,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 599,00</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<th scope=\"row\" style=\"background-color:yellow; color:black; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">Min. 15 Pax</th>\n			<td>&euro; 395,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 415,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 585,00</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<th scope=\"row\" style=\"background-color:yellow; color:black; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">Min. 20 Pax</th>\n			<td>&euro; 389,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 409,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 589,00</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<th scope=\"row\" style=\"background-color:yellow; color:black; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">Min. 25 Pax</th>\n			<td>&euro; 379,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 395,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 569,00</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<th scope=\"row\" style=\"background-color:yellow; color:black; font-weight:800;text-align: center;\">Min. 30 Pax</th>\n			<td>&euro; 369,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 385,00</td>\n			<td>&euro; 559,00</td>\n		</tr>\n	</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 255);\">TOUR EXCLUDES: </span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">International flights</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">City tax</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Turkey entry visa</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Personal expenses: Lunches, extras at the hotel or additional meals</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Tipping: Tips for guides and drivers</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Guided Istanbul Prince&#39;s Island Tour</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Istanbul (Vialand) Tour</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Guided Miniaturk Museum and Shopping Tour</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Guided Istanbul Aquarium Tour</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Insurance: All types</li>\n</ol>\n',0,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:09:03','2024-02-21 01:59:24'),(1368,6,'Special Jerusalem Tour','Special Jerusalem Tour','https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/jerusalem-tour','world-tours/jerusalem-tour','Jerusalem Tour',NULL,'juresalem.webp','World Tour','USD','0.00',12,NULL,'','','',0,0,'<h2>3 DAYS SPECIAL JERUSALEM TOUR</h2><p><img src=\"/ckeditor_images/images/Special%20Jerusalum%20Tour.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p><h2>3-DAY SPECIAL JERUSALEM TOUR ITINERARY:&nbsp;</h2><p><strong>Day 1:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Our guide will wait for you at the Ben Gurion International Airport or Land border, and lead you to our luxurious tour bus. Now we ascend to Al Quds – the Holy City of Jerusalem, the place we will have a good sized tour of Al Haram esh-Sharif, getting to know about its historic &amp; architectonical background, as nicely as the many legends informed about the holy Al Aqsa Mosque &amp; The Dome of the Rock, “whose precincts We did bless” (Al Qur’an el Kareem, Sura 17, verse 1).</p><p>We will additionally go to the Underground Mosque under the Al Aqsa, just newly opened to the public, and also to the Marawani Mosque.</p><p>Dinner and Overnight in Jerusalem</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Day 2:</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Drive to Hebron, additionally named Al-Khalil after the prophet Ibrahim. Here we will now not omit the Ibrahimi Mosque (Haram el Khalil) – a sanctuary constructed already some 2000 years in the past on the burial region of Ibrahim el Khalil, Isaac, (Nabi Yaakub), and their spouses. We will additionally seize this chance to pray at this holy place. Hebron is additionally acknowledged for its glass-blowers.</p><p>Then we drive to Bethlehem, to go to Masjid Omar close to the well-known Church of the Nativity, the place e-Nabi Issa was born Before returning to our hotel, we ascend the Mount of Olives, with its panoramic view over the Old City of Jerusalem, Maqam (Sanctuary) Rabeiah-el-Adawiyah and Suleiman el-Farsi.</p><p>Dinner and Overnight in Jerusalem</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Day 3:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>After checkout, the site of Nabi Moussa, the place medieval culture places the tomb of Nabi Moussa(Moses). Until the time of the British mandate in Palestine, this area used to be famous for “Ziyarat Nabi Moussa” which was once held right here at some stage in the spring and protected a colorful march from Jerusalem, and a week of prayers and different festive things to do then Jericho the oldest metropolis in the world town tour and get prepared for departure.</p><p>Transfer to Airport or land border</p><p>&nbsp;</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th colspan=\"3\"><strong>Rate by American dollar per person sharing a DBL room</strong></th></tr><tr><th><strong>S.S</strong></th><th><strong>230$</strong></th><th><strong>250$</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>#of passenger</th><td><strong>4**</strong></td><td><strong>4**+</strong></td></tr><tr><th>15</th><td>New Capitol or National 327</td><td>Golden walls 367</td></tr><tr><th>20+1</th><td>New Capitol or National 300</td><td>Golden walls 340</td></tr><tr><th>25+1</th><td>New Capitol or National 281</td><td>Golden walls 321</td></tr><tr><th>30+1</th><td>New Capitol or National 268</td><td>Golden walls 308</td></tr><tr><th>35+1</th><td>New Capitol or National 258</td><td>Golden walls 298</td></tr><tr><th>40+2</th><td>New Capitol or National 252</td><td>Golden walls 291</td></tr><tr><th>45+2</th><td>New Capitol or National 246</td><td>Golden walls 286</td></tr><tr><th>50+2</th><td>New Capitol or National 242</td><td>Golden walls 282</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><p>3 DAY SPECIAL JERUSALEM CITY TOUR INCLUDES:</p><ol><li>New modern buses with A/C and Wi-Fi</li><li>Professional Guide</li><li>Bottle of Water daily</li><li>Hotel accommodation on H.B</li><li>Every 20 paying get one passenger free</li><li>Each Entrance fees</li><li>Meet and assistance</li><li>Pick up or drop in Allenby Bridge border</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p>TOUR EXCLUDES:</p><ol><li>Tipping</li><li>Pick up or drop at the Taba border or Sheikh Hussein</li><li>Lunches</li><li>Insurance</li><li>Rt-PCR test</li><li>Personal expense</li><li>Visa if needed for nationalities that need visas to enter Jerusalem</li><li>Departure tax if the group needs to exit from the border from Taba or Sheikh Hussein 42$ per person</li><li>Departure tax if the group needs to exit from the border from Allenby 63$ per person</li></ol>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:09:03','2024-03-12 06:02:35'),(1369,6,'5 DAYS TASTE OF TURKEY VACATION PACKAGE','5 DAYS TASTE OF TURKEY VACATION PACKAGE','https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/5-days-taste-of-turkey-vacation-package','world-tours/5-days-taste-of-turkey-vacation-package','5 Days Taste Of Turkey Vacation Package','','','World Tour','USD','0.00',13,'','','','',0,0,'<div class=\"ramadan-packages print-hajj-packages\">\n<h1 class=\"title\">5 DAYS TASTE OF TURKEY VACATION PACKAGE</h1>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/ckeditor_images/images/5%20days%20taste%20package%20of%20turkey.jpg\" style=\"width: 100%;\" /></p>\n\n<h2><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 255);\">5 DAYS TASTE OF TURKEY VACATION PACKAGE ITINERARY:&nbsp;</span></span></h2>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><strong>Day 1:</strong>&nbsp;Istanbul - Arrival Day&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 2;\">Upon our arrival at Istanbul International Airport, your guide will meet, assist and transfer you to the hotel. Istanbul was the capital city of the Byzantium &amp; Roman Empires and the Ottoman State. It is a most fascinating city, which actually crosses two continents Europe and Asia. It is a city of amalgamation of museums, bazaars, minarets, mosques, churches, palaces, and restaurants catering to everyone&rsquo;s taste, customs, and fifteen million people. Overnight in Istanbul.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><strong>Day 2:</strong>&nbsp;Istanbul City Tour</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Very rich continental open buffet Breakfast included)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 2;\">Aft After breakfast, we have Istanbul City Tour. Our first visit will be to HIPPODROME. Ancient Hippodrome was the scene of chariot races, with three monuments; the Obelisk of Theodosius, the bronze Serpentine Column and the Column of Constantine. Then we will visit SULTANAHMET IMPERIAL MOSQUE. Across from Hagia Sophia Grand Mosque, it was built in the 16th century by the architect Mehmet, is known as the BLUE MOSQUE because of its magnificent interior decoration of blue Iznik tiles. Our next visit will be to HAGIA SOPHIA GRAND MOSQUE. The Hagia Sophia Grand Mosque, previously known as the Church of Divine Wisdom, is simply the best of its kind! Hagia Sophia Grand Mosque is the greatest surviving example of Byzantine Architecture. For 1000 years, it was once the largest church in the world, decorated with stunning 6th-century golden mosaics. Today it is a mosque. Lunch break at 13:00 pm. After lunch, TravelShop Group will take you to the ASIL EFENDI which is a unique atmosphere with reasonable prices for your shopping. Here you will find; Exotic Spices and Herbs, Turkish Baklava, Turkish Delights, Turkish Coffee, nuts and fruits, small souvenirs such as Ceramic Handicrafts, Evil Eyes totems, all-natural olive oil, soaps, and many other goods in Souvenir Shops and stores. After the tour, transfer back to your hotel. Overnight in Istanbul.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Note:</strong>&nbsp; Please do not forget to carry a headscarf with you for the visit to religious places such as Blue Mosque &amp; Hagia Sophia Mosque. &nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><strong>Day 3:</strong>&nbsp;Istanbul Bosphorus Cruise and Flight to Cappadocia</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Very rich continental open buffet Breakfast included)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 2;\">After breakfast enjoys BOSPORUS BY BOAT; a traditional excursion by boat along the waterway separating Europe and Asia. The shore is lined with old wooden villas, palaces of marble, fortresses, and small fishing villages. During the excursion, you will see the magnificent sights of the following attractions from your boat. See Dolmabahce Palace, and further along, the parks and imperial pavilions of Yildiz Palace. On the coastal edge of this park, is Ciragan Palace, 300 meters of its marble facade faces the shore. At Ortakoy a great variety of artists, gather every Sunday to display their work along the street. Ortakoy is a symbol of tolerance with a church, a mosque, and a synagogue existing side by side for centuries. RUMELI FORTRESS (view from the boat), Built by Mehmet the Conqueror in 1452 prior to the conquest of Istanbul was completed in only four months to control and protect the infamous Bosporus passage. It is one of the most beautiful works of military architecture anywhere in the world. BEYLERBEYI PALACE (view from the boat), is the summer residence of Ottoman sultans and exists in its original renovated glory featuring original antique furniture and magnificent gardens with the Harem on the Asian side of Istanbul. Lunch break at the Turkish restaurant. After lunch, we will then take you to the GRAND SPICE BAZAAR, which is a unique atmosphere with reasonable prices for your shopping. Here you will find; Exotic Spices and Herbs, Turkish Baklava, Turkish Delights, Turkish Coffee, nuts and fruits, small souvenirs such as Ceramic Handicrafts, Evil Eyes totems, all-natural olive oil, soaps, and many other goods in Souvenir Shops and stores. After the tour transfer to Istanbul Airport for a domestic flight to Cappadocia. Transfer from the airport and check in to your hotel in Cappadocia. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia.</span><br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; text-align: justify;\">Note:</strong><span style=\"font-size: 14px; text-align: justify;\">&nbsp; If you wish to join our optional activity of Cappadocia Hor Air Ballooning tomorrow, please contact your guide and register because it will take place early the next morning.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><strong>Day 4:</strong>Cappadocia Underground City &amp; Goreme Open Air Museum</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Very rich continental open buffet Breakfast included)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 2;\">After breakfast at 09:30 depart for Cappadocia Tour. We will drive you to Ozkonak Underground City, one of the best-preserved Underground cities in Cappadocia. After the Underground City tour, you visit the Goreme Open Air Museum, the Heart of Cappadocia. Goreme Open Air Museum is famous for frescoes dating to the 10th century describing the life of Jesus Christ and monks. The next stop is Cavusin, which is an abandoned village with old cave Greek houses. After Cavusin you go to the restaurant in Avanos to have lunch. After lunch, you visit a pottery workshop, to see how to make pottery. Then you go to Love Valley. Love Valley Cappadocia is a hidden valley with scenic formations, to say the least. Despite the resemblance to manhood, these amazing rock formations are far from man-made. The next stop is Devrent Valley, which is also called Imagination Valley, where you can see natural rock formations looking like animals. The last stop is Three Beauties, three beautiful fairy chimneys with their hats, which is the symbol of Cappadocia. This tour will end approximately at 18.00 and you will be returned back to your hotel. Dinner and Overnight in Cappadocia.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><strong>Day 5:</strong>Cappadocia to Istanbul - End of the Tour</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Very rich continental open buffet Breakfast included)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 2;\">After breakfast, you will have free time in Cappadocia. Today we will depart for Kayseri Airport for our domestic flight to Istanbul and then back home. We hope your tour was a memorable one and we would like to see you in the future on one of our tours again. Have a nice trip back home and thanks for choosing TravelShop Booking.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 255);\">5 DAYS TASTE OF TURKEY VACATION PACKAGE INCLUDES:</span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">All airport transfer services mentioned in the itinerary</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Arrival airport transfer to Kayseri / Nevsehir airport</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">2 nights hotel in Istanbul</li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justif