val at Haydar Aliyev International Airport.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Greetings from the company representative.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&ldquo;Flames of Baku&rdquo; night excursion.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The tour begins from Upland Park which overlooks an astonishing view of a nightlife town glowing with vibrant lights. Upland Park is placed on an excessive hill in the western section of the city. It is a great spot to look at the town itself and Baku Bay.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Night promenade on Baku Boulevard beginning from Flag Square and passing by means of the Baku Ferris Wheel. Seaside Boulevard is one of the most important sights of the capital. This over-100-year-old sightseeing is a favorite entertainment location of residents and visitors of Baku.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The tour ends with a taking walks tour of Torgovy Street and Fountains Square. In the center of the XIX century, the avenue gained the title of Torgovy (trade) due to its favorable region and abundance of alternate stores there.&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Overnight at the hotel.</span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Day 2: Baku City Tour</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Breakfast at the hotel.&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Baku City tour.&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Avenue of Martyrs.&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Highland Park.&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Walking tour via Old City.&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Tour through Baku Boulevard.&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Walking tour via Nizami Street.&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Visiting Haydar Aliyev Centre (photostop).&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Zaha Hadid Architects was once appointed as the design architect of the Heydar Aliyev Center following opposition in 2007. The Center, designed to come to be the major construction for the nation&rsquo;s cultural programs, breaks from the inflexible and regularly enormous Soviet structure that is so customary in Baku, aspiring rather to specific the sensibilities of Azeri tradition and the optimism of a kingdom that appears to the future.&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Overnight at Baku.&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><strong>Day 3: Absheron Tour</strong></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Breakfast at the Hotel.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Absheron tour.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Trip to Ateshgah, a fireplace worshipper&rsquo;s temple positioned in Surakhany contract and constructed by means of Indian retailers touring via the Great Silk Route. The temple is one of the many warning signs of the existence of Zoroastrianism in ancient Azerbaijan.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Trip to Yanardagh burning Mount positioned on the city outskirts. From the fifth century on Yanardagh had been referred to in historic ancient books.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Shopping.</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Overnight at Baku.</span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Day 4: Transfer</span></strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Breakfast at the hotel.&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Departure from the lodge (3 hours earlier than the flight).&nbsp;</span></li>\n	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Airport transfer.&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 255);\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Azerbaijan Tour Package service&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Rehman Travels provides&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/visa/azerbaijan-visa\">Azerbaijan visit visas</a>&nbsp;at affordable rates. We have different&nbsp;</span><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; --tw-border-spacing-x: 0; --tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); --tw