east Asia and it is an island city. It is a hub of education, healthcare, finance, tourism, and entertainment across the world. Singapore is also known as Lion City. Singaporean food is very famous and an amazing attraction for tourists and food lovers. Mass Rapid Transit (MRT) and Light Rail Transit (LRT) are mostly used in Singapore for transportation. Book the <a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/singapore-tour\">Singapore Tour package</a> and explore beautiful places with Rehman Travels.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Visa Policy for&nbsp;Singapore</p><p>Singapore has a policy to issue visas to four types of travel purposes which are for Tourism, Business, Study, and Diplomatic visas.</p><h2>&nbsp; &nbsp; Singapore Tourist Visa</h2><ul><li>Singapore Work Visa</li><li>Singapore Permanent Residence Visa</li><li>Singapore Diplomatic Visa</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Singapore Visit Visa Requirements</p><ul><li>Scan Copy of Passport.</li><li>Passport Sign Page.</li><li>CNIC Scan Copy.</li><li>Bank statement and employment letter</li><li>01 Photos Scan Copy White Background.</li><li>8 Working Days</li></ul><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Singapore Visit Visa Terms &amp; Conditions</h4><ul><li>Visa fee once deposited shall NOT BE refunded in case of visa application is rejected/denied by the authorities in Singapore.</li><li>All visitors should have a valid return ticket and a passport valid for a minimum period of six months</li><li>However, visa regulations and costs are subject to change</li><li>Visa Approval is Subject to Immigration.</li><li>&nbsp;Rehman Travels is not responsible in case of Visa is rejected/delayed, visa fee is Non-Refundable in any case.</li><li>Over-staying in Singapore your visa will result in fines and detentions.</li><li>The Embassy/ Immigration of Singapore recommends all their eligible applicants to strictly follow the Rules and Regulations in order to avoid any delay.&nbsp;</li><li>Since the visa policy is being monitored by the Singapore authorities, therefore, the instructions provided by the Embassy are subject to change without any prior notification.</li></ul><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Visa Requirements for Official &amp; Diplomatic Passport holder</h4><ul><li>Note Verbal of older dates will not be accepted</li><li>The Purpose of Entry should be mentioned on the note verbal and the VISA FORM</li><li>Incomplete Applications will NOT be entertained&nbsp;</li><li>For diplomatic missions, UN agencies &amp; international organizations in Islamabad</li><li>Note Verbal from the concerned Mission/ Office is compulsory&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Singapore Visit Visa Services</h2><p>Rehman Travels provides the Singapore visit visas and <a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/\">hotel bookings</a> at affordable rates for Travelers around the globe. Traveling with us will take your imagination with reality &amp; you can get an opportunity to enjoy and explore the natural beauty of Singapore.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Singapore Visit Visa Fee</h2><p>Singapore Visit Visa fee from Pakistan is Rs 14000 and it varies from country to country and changes with time. For updated Singapore Visa fee consult Rehman Travels visa consultation department. Our services are available 24/7 at +92 (0) 51 111 786 785.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Best Time to Visit Singapore</h2><p>The best time to visit Singapore is between February and April. Book <a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/flights\">flight from Islamabad to Singapore</a> at cheap rates</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Things to do in Singapore</h3><p>Many attractive places to visit in Singapore are Sentosa, Gardens by the Bay, Singapore Zoo, Singapore Flyer, Merlion, Singapore Botanic Gardens, River Safari, Singapore Cable Car, National Museum of Singapore, Mount Faber, Sultan Mosque, Skyline Luge, Wings of Time, and Science Center Singapore.&nbsp;</p><p>Night Safari is the world’s first nocturnal zoo and attracts tourists all over the world. Orchard Road is the main shopping area where hotels, shops, boutiques, and eateries are the main attractions.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Singapore Travel Tips</h3><ul><li>Use public transport</li><li>Eat food from local markets like Hawker Center</li><li>Check the weather condition</li><li>Avoid bottled water</li><li>Budget Shopping at Bugis Street, Mustafa Center, and Far East Plaza</li><li>Travel Itinerary</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>FAQs</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Is snow occurring in Singapore?</h4><p>No, snow is not occurring in Singapore. In November, December, and January the weather is very cold and rain occurs. Some places in Singapore where you enjoy snowfall like Snow City (Hansel and Gretel’s Winter Adventure), Christmas Wonderland, Raffles City Singapore, Tanglin Mall, and Orchard Central.&nbsp;</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Is transportation expensive in Singapore?</h4><p>Yes, transportation is not very expensive in Singapore. Public transport is very cheap in Singapore which every traveler can afford. The easiest way to explore Singapore is via the metro. If you have a Singapore tourist pass you get unlimited rides on the bus and metro. Travel in Singapore that is not possible by bus or metro use a taxi for travel.&nbsp;</p><h3>Which language is spoken in Singapore?</h3><p>English, Malay, Mandarin, and Tamil languages are spoken in Singapore. Malay is the national language of Singapore. English is spoken in Singapore but at first, it is difficult for foreigners to understand because their English is a combination of English and Malay. So try to learn a few words of their national language to communicate with them easily.</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Is food expensive in Singapore?</h4><p>Food is not expensive in Singapore. Get a good meal in Singapore at a very low price but depends on where you eat and what you eat. You can easily buy cheap food from the food streets, food courts, and hawker stalls. They served excellent meals at a very low cost. Hotels and restaurants are a little expensive but it also depends on what you eat.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Note:</h4><p><strong>Visa&nbsp;</strong>Approval is&nbsp; Subjected to Singapore&nbsp; Immigration,&nbsp; Rehman Travels is not responsible in case of Visa is rejected / Delayed, The Visa fee is&nbsp; <strong>Non-Refundable</strong> in any case. Kindly note and advise your Client&nbsp; Accordingly.</p>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:29:34','2024-02-26 20:32:02'),(1376,4,'Dubai Visa | Dubai Visa fees | Dubai Visit Visa |  UAE Visa','Dubai visa fee from Pakistan, Dubai visit visa from Pakistan, Dubai visit visa cost, Dubai visit visa requirements, e visa Dubai, Dubai transit visa by RGT','https://www.rehmantravel.com/visa/dubai/','visa/dubai','Dubai Visit Visa',NULL,'Dubai.webp','Visa','USD','160',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,'',0,1,'<p>Are you ready to experience the magic of Dubai? Plan your visit hassle-free with our Dubai Visit Visa services. From the iconic Burj Khalifa to the enchanting desert landscapes, Dubai has something for everyone. Whether you\'re a tourist, reuniting with family, or exploring business opportunities, your visa needs are covered.</p><h2>Dubai Visit Visa Requirements</h2><p>Look at the below table and understand the Dubai visa online requirements.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Valid Passport:</strong> Your passport should be valid for at least six months from the date of entry into Dubai.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Visa Application Form:</strong> Complete the Dubai visa application form accurately. This is often provided by the visa sponsor.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Passport-Sized Photos:</strong> Provide recent passport-sized photographs as per the specifications outlined by the authorities. Flight Reservation: Submit a copy of your round-trip flight reservation. This indicates your intention to leave Dubai after the visit.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Accommodation Details:</strong> Provide proof of your accommodation arrangements in Dubai. This could be a hotel reservation or an address where you will be staying.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Travel Itinerary:</strong> Include a detailed travel itinerary, outlining your planned activities during your stay in Dubai.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Proof of Financial Means:</strong> Demonstrate your ability to financially support yourself during your stay. This could include bank statements, pay stubs, or a letter of sponsorship.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Sponsorship Letter:</strong> If you have a sponsor in Dubai, such as a relative or a company, a sponsorship letter is often required. This letter should include the sponsor\'s details and confirmation of their willingness to take responsibility for your stay.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>No Objection Certificate (NOC):</strong> Some applicants may need to provide a No Objection Certificate (NOC) from their employer, stating that the employer has no objections to the individual visiting Dubai.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Health Insurance:</strong> Health insurance is recommended to cover any unforeseen medical expenses during your stay.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Visa Fee:</strong> Pay the applicable visa fee. The fee varies depending on the type and duration of the visa.</p><p>It\'s important to note that the specific requirements may vary based on the visit visa type and individual circumstances.</p><h3>Apply For a Dubai Visit Visa</h3><p>Here is a general guide on how to apply for a Dubai visit visa from Pakistan:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Step 1: Identify Your Sponsor:</strong> To apply for a Dubai visa online, you typically need a sponsor, such as a resident, a company, or a hotel in Dubai. The sponsor will initiate the visa application process on your behalf.</p><p>The sponsor has three different types, which include:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Individual Sponsor:</strong> If you have a family member or friend residing in Dubai, they can act as your sponsor.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Company Sponsor:</strong> If you are visiting Dubai for business purposes, your employer or a business in Dubai can sponsor your visit.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Hotel Sponsor:</strong> Hotels can also act as sponsors for tourists. You may need to make a reservation with a hotel that offers this service.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Step 2: Gather Required Documents:</strong> Collect the necessary documents for the visa application. This may include:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><ol><li>Passport copy (valid for at least six months)</li><li>Passport-sized photos</li><li>Completed visa application form</li><li>Flight reservation details</li><li>Accommodation reservation details</li><li>Travel itinerary</li><li>Proof of financial means (bank statements, pay stubs, etc.)</li><li>Sponsorship letter and/or No Objection Certificate (if applicable)</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Step 3: Sponsor Initiates the Application:</strong> The sponsor will typically be responsible for initiating the visa application process. They may need to visit the relevant immigration or visa service center in Dubai.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Step 4: Application Submission:</strong> The sponsor will submit your application and the required documents to the appropriate authorities. This can often be done online or in person.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Step 5: Visa Processing:</strong> The visa processing time can vary, but you should receive updates on the status of your application. Once approved, the visa will be stamped on your passport.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Step 6: Travel to Dubai&nbsp;</strong> With your approved Dubai Visit Visa, you can travel to Dubai on the specified dates. Make sure to adhere to the visa conditions, including the duration of stay and any other specific guidelines.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Dubai Visit Visa Processing Time</h4><p>Generally, the processing time for a Dubai Visit Visa can range from a few days to a few weeks. Some factors that may influence the processing time include:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Type of Visa:</strong> Different types of visas (tourist visa, family visit visa, business visa, etc.) may have varying processing times.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Sponsorship:</strong> The time it takes for the sponsor to initiate and submit the application can impact the overall processing time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Completeness of Documentation:</strong> Applications with all the required documents in order are likely to be processed more efficiently.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Government Policies:</strong> Changes in immigration policies or procedures can affect processing times.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Peak Seasons:</strong> During peak travel seasons, there may be higher demand for visas, potentially leading to slightly longer processing times.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Dubai Visit Visa Price</h4><p>For visiting Dubai, the visa fees often depend on the type and duration of the visa. Here is a general guideline of the Dubai visa price:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>30-Day Dubai Tourist Visa</strong></p><p>• This is a common short-term visa for tourism purposes.</p><p>• The cost might vary but is generally starting from AED 350 to AED 400.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>90-Day Dubai Tourist Visa</strong></p><p>• This visa allows for a longer stay, usually up to 90 days.</p><p>• The cost may be higher, starting from AED 900 to AED 1,500 or more.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Multiple Entry Dubai Tourist Visa</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>• Some visas allow multiple entries within a specified period.</p><p>• The fees for multiple entry visas can vary, starting from AED 1,000 or more.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>E Visa Dubai</h4><p>The e-visa allows travelers to apply for and obtain a visa online before arriving in Dubai. However, it\'s crucial to note that visa policies and procedures may change, so it\'s advisable to check for the latest information.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here is a general overview of the e-visa process for Dubai:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Types of E-Visas:</strong> Dubai offers various types of e-Visas, including tourist visas, visit visas, and transit visas.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Eligibility:</strong> The eligibility criteria for e-Visas may vary based on the type of visa and the nationality of the traveler.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Application Process:</strong> Travelers can typically apply for an e-Visa through the official online portal of the General Directorate of Residency and Foreigners Affairs (GDRFA) of Dubai or the UAE\'s official visa application platform.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Required Documents:</strong> The necessary documents for the e-Visa application may include a passport with a minimum validity period, a passport-sized photograph, proof of accommodation, and a return flight ticket.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Processing Time:</strong> The processing time for e-Visas may vary, but it is generally processed within a few days.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Fees:</strong> The fees for e-visas depend on the type of visa and its duration. The fees can starting from AED 250 to AED 1,000 or more.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Validity Period:</strong> The validity of e-Visas can vary. Tourist visas may be valid for 30 or 90 days, while other types of visas may have different durations</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Dubai Transit Visa</h4><p>The transit visa allows travelers to stay in Dubai for a short duration before continuing their journey to their final destination.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here are some general points about Dubai transit visas:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Eligibility:</strong> Transit visas are typically available for passengers who have a layover in Dubai and meet certain eligibility criteria.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Duration of Stay:</strong> The duration of stay with a transit visa is usually short, allowing passengers to spend a specific number of hours or days in Dubai.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Application Process</strong>: Travelers can often apply for a transit visa through the official online portal of the General Directorate of Residency and Foreigners Affairs (GDRFA) of Dubai or the UAE\'s official visa application platform.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Required Documents:</strong> The necessary documents may include a valid passport, a confirmed onward flight ticket, and proof of the layover duration.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Fees:</strong> Transit Dubai visa fees may apply, and the cost can vary depending on factors such as the duration of stay. The fees are usually lower compared to tourist visas.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Processing Time:</strong> The processing time for transit visas is generally quicker compared to other types of visas, and travelers can usually obtain approval within a short period</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Dubai Tourist Visa</h4><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Tourist visas allow travelers to stay in Dubai for a specified period and are subject to certain terms and conditions. Keep in mind that Dubai tourist visa requirements can change, so it\'s essential to check the Dubai visa official website or consult with us.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>To apply for the Dubai tourist visa, take a look below and learn about it:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Types of Tourist Visas:</strong> Dubai offers various types of tourist visas, including short-term tourist visas for 30 days and long-term tourist visas for 90 days.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Eligibility: </strong>Tourist visas are typically available to individuals who intend to visit Dubai for tourism purposes. Eligibility may vary based on factors such as nationality.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Application Process:</strong> Travelers can apply for a tourist visa through the official online portal of the General Directorate of Residency and Foreigners Affairs (GDRFA) of Dubai or the UAE\'s official visa application platform.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Required Documents: </strong>Commonly required documents for a Dubai visitor visa include a valid passport, passport-sized photographs, proof of accommodation, proof of financial means, and a return flight ticket.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Fees: </strong>A Dubai tourist visa price varies based on the type and duration of the visa. The cost can starting from AED 350 to AED 1,500 or more.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Processing Time:</strong> The processing time for a Dubai travel visa can vary, but it is generally processed within a few days.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Validity Period:</strong> Tourist visas are typically valid for either 30 or 90 days, depending on the type of visa and the traveler\'s preference.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>FAQs</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>How to apply for an online Dubai visit visa from Pakistan?</h4><p>To apply for an online Dubai visit visa from Pakistan, visit the official website of the General Directorate of Residency and Foreigners Affairs (GDRFA) Dubai or use the UAE\'s official visa application platform, and follow the specified application process, providing the required documents and paying the applicable fees.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>How long does it take to process a Dubai visit visa from Pakistan?</h4><p>The processing time for a Dubai visit visa from Pakistan can vary, but it is generally processed within a few days, often ranging from 3 to 5 working days.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Can I extend my Dubai visit visa?</h4><p>The recent rules allow travelers to add 30 or 60 more days to their visit visas while staying in the country. However, the total time you can stay in the country within a year cannot exceed 120 days, so you can\'t extend your visa beyond this limit.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>How to apply for a Dubai tourist visa?</h4><p>To apply for a Dubai tourist visa, follow these steps:</p><ul><li>Complete the application form</li><li>Submit required documents</li><li>Pay the applicable fees.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>How i can get an e-visa to Dubai?</h4><ul><li>To obtain an e-Visa for Dubai, you should do these steps:</li><li>Visit the official website of the General Directorate of Residency and Foreigners Affairs (GDRFA) Dubai or use the UAE\'s official visa application platform