Indonesia has beautiful beaches, museums, and islands.&nbsp;</p><h2>Visa policy for Indonesia&nbsp;</h2><p>Indonesia has a visa policy to issue visas to four types of travel purposes which are for Tourism, Business, Study, Diplomatic, and Journalist visas.</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Indonesia Tourist Visa</p><ul><li>Indonesia Journalist Visa</li><li>Indonesia Diplomatic Visa&nbsp;</li><li>Indonesia Limited Stay Visa</li></ul><h2>Indonesia E Visa Requirements for Pakistani</h2><ul><li>Passport 1st Page Scan</li><li>Picture White Background Scan</li><li>CNIC Scan</li><li>Vaccination Card</li></ul><p>Indonesia Visit Visa Terms &amp; Condition</p><ul><li>Visa fee once deposited shall NOT BE refunded in case of visa application is rejected/denied by the authorities in Indonesia.</li><li>All visitors should have a valid return ticket and a passport valid for a minimum period of six months.</li><li>However, visa regulations and costs are subject to change</li><li>Visa Approval is Subject to Immigration Rehman Travels is not responsible in case of Visa is rejected/delayed, the visa fee is Non-Refundable in any case.</li><li>Overstaying in Indonesia your visa will result in fines and detentions.</li><li>The Embassy/ Immigration of Indonesia recommends all their eligible applicants to strictly follow the Rules and Regulations in order to avoid any delay.&nbsp;</li><li>Since the visa policy is being monitored by the Indonesian authorities, therefore, the instructions provided by the Embassy are subject to change without any prior notification.</li></ul><h2>Indonesia Visit Visa Services</h2><p>Indonesia offers visa-free entry for a number of countries and in addition, Indonesia also has the visa on arrival facility for certain nationalities. Visitors from all other countries have to obtain a visa from the Indonesian Embassy in their respective countries. Pakistan nationals require a visa prior to departure for Indonesia.</p><p>Rehman Group of Travel offers all types of visa processing facilities for Indonesia. Rehman Travel also caters the <a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/\">hotel bookings</a> and travel packages at very competitive rates for all 5-star and budget travelers.</p><h2>Indonesia Visit Visa Fee</h2><p>Indonesia Visit Visa fee for Pakistani nationals is $85 per person and this price varies from country to country and changes with time. Consult Rehman Travels for an Indonesia Visit Visa. Our services are available 24/7 at +92 (0) 51 111 786 785.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><h3>Things to do in Indonesia</h3><p>Indonesia has many awe-inspiring and breathtaking places for tourists and travelers like Tanah Lot, Uluwatu Temple, Borobudur Temple, Gili Island, Mount Batur, Nusa Lembongan, Goa Gajah, Gili Trawangan, Komodo National Park, Lake Toba, Gili Air, National monument, West Bali National Park, Kawah Putih and other attractive places.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><h3>Indonesia Travel Tips</h3><ul><li>Must try Indonesian Food</li><li>Visit Bali Safari and Marine Park</li><li>Learn some words of the Indonesian language</li><li>Explore Bali and Java Island</li><li>Return Ticket</li><li>Valid Passport</li><li>Eat street food</li><li>Pay with cash not using a credit card</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>FAQs</p><h4>What is the best time to visit Indonesia?</h4><p>May and September are the best time to visit Indonesia because the days are dry and sunny. In October and April, the weather is very wet and rainfall occurs. Some regions in Indonesia where rainfall occurs in June and July. November to March the temperature is humid. In the monsoon season, visiting islands is a little risky.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Is accommodation cheap in Indonesia?</h4><p>Accommodation in Indonesia is not very expensive. You can easily find a good place to stay at a cheap price. Many low-cost hotels with good services are available in Indonesia for visitors. Find good deals on the internet for hotels and book them in advance. You can easily afford accommodation in Indonesia.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Visa on arrival for Pakistani?</h4><p>No, Pakistan is not eligible for Indonesia visa on arrival. Apply for an Indonesian visa from Pakistan by visiting the Indonesian embassy or consult Rehman Travel. Submit the complete documents to the travel agent or Indonesian embassy for an Indonesian visa. Visa applicants of Punjab applying in Islamabad for an Indonesia Visa should submit the character certificate.&nbsp;</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>What is the processing time of the Indonesia visa?</h4><p>Processing time for Indonesia Visa is 7 to 8 days. If you are traveling to different regions of Indonesia like Poso and Maluku, then you will require a written permission from the Indonesian government through the Jakarta Department of Foreign Affairs. A tourist visa for Indonesia is issued to the traveler for the visiting purposes, attending a seminar, meeting, or event.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:29:34','2024-02-26 20:41:02'),(1378,4,'Kenya Visit visa | Kenya visit visa fee | Kenya e Visa','Kenya tourist visa, e visa Kenya, Kenya visa from Pakistan, Kenya visa online, Kenya visit visa fee, Kenya visa requirements, Kenya visa by rehmantravel.com',NULL,'visa/kenya-visa','Kenya Visit Visa',NULL,NULL,'Visa','USD','0.00',15,NULL,'','','',0,0,'<h2>Kenya visit visa from Pakistan</h2><p>Kenya is an East African country. Nairobi is the capital of Kenya. The population of Kenya is more than 52.2 million and it is the world’s 48th largest country by total area. Kenya is the main hub of East Africa in financial, economic, and transport. June to November is the best season to visit Kenya because in these months the weather is cooler and season of short rain.&nbsp;</p><h2>Kenya Tourist Visa</h2><ul><li>Kenya Single Entry Visa<ul><li>Issued to single or multiple persons and used by businessmen and tourists.</li></ul></li><li>Kenya Transit Visa<ul><li>Issued for three days and for those whose nationalities require a visa for Kenya and who move via