s in Sri Lanka that attract tourists.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><h3>Travel Tips for Sri Lanka Travel</h3><ul><li>Money Exchange</li><li>Use local transport (Tuk Tuks)</li><li>Check weather before travel</li><li>Must try Sri Lankan food</li><li><a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/flights\">Airline Tickets</a></li><li>Travel Itinerary</li></ul><p>FAQs&nbsp;</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Is Sri Lanka a safe country?</h4><p>Yes, Sri Lanka is a safe country for tourists. SriLankan Tourism Promotion Bureau announced that all the tourism activities and the places are safe for tourists. But beware of the robbers and the thieves. Srilanka transport is also very safe for travelers.&nbsp; The best time to visit Srilanka west coast is from December to March and the east coast from April to September.&nbsp;</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Is Pakistani food easily available in Sri Lanka?</h4><p>Yes, many hotels and restaurants served Pakistani/halal food in Sri Lanka. Food is not expensive in Sri Lanka. Even many luxury hotels and restaurants also served good quality meals at a reasonable price. In Sri Lanka food street, you can easily eat delicious food and at a very cheap price. Whereas Sri Lankan food is also good in taste.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Is Sri Lanka an expensive country?</h4><p>Sri Lanka is a cheap country. Accommodation, transportation, and food is not very expensive in Sri Lanka. Travelers normally used tuk-tuks for travel. It can be expensive but depends on where you stay, what you eat, and which transport you used. Shopping in Sri Lanka attracts tourists so always shop from the local shops.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>What are the best safari places in Sri Lanka?</h4><p>Sri Lanka is famous for wildlife Safari. The best <a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/world-tours/kandy-nuwaraeliya\">Safari places to visit in Sri Lanka</a>&nbsp;are:</p><ul><li>Yala National Park</li><li>Mannar Island</li><li>Udawalawe National Park</li><li>Wasgamuwa National Park</li><li>Horton Plains National Park</li><li>Wilpattu National Park</li><li>Bundala National Park</li><li>Minneriya National Park</li><li>Kaudulla National Park</li><li>Kanneliya National Park&nbsp;</li></ul>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:29:34','2024-02-26 20:45:07'),(1380,4,'Tajikistan visit visa | Tajikistan visa | Tajikistan e visa','Tajikistan tourist visa, Tajikistan evisa, Tajikistan visa requirements, Tajikistan visa price & Tajikistan online visa & visa consultancy by rehmantravel.com','https://www.rehmantravel.com/visa/tajikistan-visa','visa/tajikistan-visa','Tajikistan Visit Visa',NULL,'tajikistan.webp','Visa','USD','0.00',4,NULL,'','','',0,0,'<p>Tajikistan is surrounded by, Kyrgyzstan, China, Uzbekistan, and Afghanistan. Tajikistan is famous for hiking and climbing. Tajikistan culture is very similar to Afghanistan and Iran. Pamir highway is the second highest road in the world and very famous in Tajikistan. Handicrafts like ceramics, suzani, wooden products, and kundal paintings are very famous in Tajikistan.</p><h3>Tajikistan Visa Policy</h3><p>Tajikistan has a policy to issue visa to four type of travel purpose which are for Tourism, Business, Study and Diplomatic visa.</p><h2>&nbsp; &nbsp; Tajikistan Tourist Visa</h2><ul><li>Tajikistan Business Visa</li><li>Tajikistan Diplomatic Visa</li><li>Tajikistan Student Visa</li></ul><h2>Tajikistan Visit Visa Requirements</h2><ul><li>Passport Scan Copy.</li><li>1 Passport Size Photo\'s Scan Copy.</li><li>CNIC Photo Copy.</li><li>Passport Sign Page.</li><li>5-6 Working Days Required.</li></ul><h2>Tajikistan E Visa</h2><p>Travel to Tajikistan on E-Visa. Enter the Tajikistan you need an E-Visa. Get Tajikistan E-Visa in three steps.&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Apply for Tajikistan E Visa</li><li>Pay for Tajikistan E Visa</li><li>Get Tajikistan E Visa&nbsp;</li></ul><h3>Things to do in Tajikistan</h3><p>Tajikistan is a mountainous country and many amazing sightseeing places in Tajikistan are Lenin Peak, Iskanderkul, Ismoil Somoni Peak, Sarez Lake, Korzhenevskoi Peak, Yashilkul, Bulunkul, Nurek Dam, Pamir National Park, Fedchenko Glacier, Tajikistan National Museum, Chimtarga, Safed Dara, Karl Marx Peak, Kokhi Navruz, Seven Lakes, Ozero Rangkul, Dushanbe Zoo, Engels Peak, Luchob Park, and Pik Sat.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><h4>Best time to Visit Tajikistan</h4><p>June to mid-September is the best time to visit Tajikistan.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Tajikistan Travel Tips</h4><ul><li>Use local transport</li><li>Valid Passport</li><li><a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/flights\">Return Ticket</a></li><li>Travel itinerary</li><li>Learn a few words of Tajik language</li><li>Must visit Pamir highway</li><li>Use bottled water</li></ul><p>FYI</p><p>Rehman travels also provide the facility for travel insurance and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/flights\">cheap flights to Dushanbe</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>FAQs</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Tajikistan embassy in Pakistan?</h4><p>Tajikistan embassy is located in Islamabad. Tajik embassy is offering its services to all the people who are interested to go to Tajikistan for tourism or other purposes.&nbsp;</p><p>Address: House 295, Street No. 35, Sector F 11/3 Islamabad, Pakistan</p><p>Telephone: 92 51 2293462</p><p>You can also consult rehman travel consultants for <a href=\"https://www.rehmantravel.com/site/contactUs\">complete guide for tajikistan visit visa</a></p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Can easily rent a car in Tajikistan?</h4><p>Yes, you can easily rent a car in Tajikistan but with a driver. It is always prefered to use the car with driver as the local rules are implemented and one should always try to avoid any unnecessary involment which may lead to any palenty due to lack of awarness of trafic ules.</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Do people speak English in Tajikistan?</h4><p>Yes, people speak English in Tajikistan, Along with the English langueage many other local and international languages like Russian, Tajik and Persion are spoken and understood in Tajikistan. People usually dont find any language barrier while visiting Tajikistan</p><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>Is E-Visa used in Tajikistan?</h4><p>E-Visa is used in Tajikistan. E-Visa is used for traveling in Tajikistan. One have to get the e visa for Tajikistan before arrival on international airports of tajikistan.</p>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:29:34','2024-02-26 20:11:44'),(1381,4,'Thailand visit visa | Thailand visa | Thailand e visa | Visa','Thailand tourist visa, Thailand evisa, Thailand visa requirements, Thailand visa price & Thailand visa online consultancy by rehmantravel.com',NULL,'visa/thailand-visa','Thailand Visit Visa',NULL,NULL,'Visa','USD','0.00',1,NULL,'','','',0,0,'<h2><strong>Thailand Visit Visa</strong></h2><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Embark on a seamless journey to the enchanting land of Thailand with Rehman Travels. Discover the vibrant culture, pristine beaches, and captivating landscapes hassle-free, as we assist you in securing your Thailand visit visa. Whether you\'re planning a short getaway or an extended stay, our expert team ensures a smooth and efficient visa application process.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Our services are tailored to meet your specific travel needs, offering a range of visa options, including Tourist Visa, Visa on Arrival, Multiple Entry Tourist Visa, and Long-Stay Visa.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Begin your journey with confidence – apply for your Thailand visit visa today with Rehman Travels!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Thailand Visa Policy</h2><p>&nbsp;</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Thailand Visa Type</strong></th><th><strong>Visa Type</strong></th><th><strong>Validity of Visa</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"2\"><strong>Thailand Non-Immigrant Visa</strong></td><td>Non-Immigrant Visa Single Entry</td><td>3 months</td></tr><tr><td>Non-Immigrant Visa Multiple Entry</td><td>1 year / 3 years</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"2\"><strong>Thailand Tourist Visa</strong></td><td>Tourist Visa Single Entry</td><td>3 months</td></tr><tr><td>Tourist Visa Multiple Entry</td><td>6 months</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"3\"><strong>Thailand Transit Visa</strong></td><td>Transit Visa Single Entry</td><td>3 months</td></tr><tr><td>Transit Visa Double Entry</td><td>3 months / 6 months</td></tr><tr><td>Transit Visa Triple Entry</td><td>3 months / 6 months</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Note: The time/period of stay is determined by Thai Immigration.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>90 Days</p><h4>NON-B Business Visa</h4><p>Single Entry <strong>PKR 29500 /-</strong>Per Person</p><p>REQUIREMENT</p><ul><li>Thai National ID Card</li><li>Invitation letter from Company</li><li>Company Registration</li><li>Company Tax Return</li><li>DBDs Files</li><li>Bank Statement&nbsp;</li><li>Account Maintenance</li><li>Pictures</li><li>Passport (previous passport)</li><li>NTN No</li><li>Company letter Head.</li><li>Multi Entry 1 Year 67000/- Per Person</li></ul><p>90 Days</p><h4>NON-O Family Visa</h4><p>Single Entry <strong>PKR 29500 /-</strong>Per Person</p><p>REQUIREMENTS</p><ul><li>If the wife is a Thai National</li><li>Invitation letter from the wife</li><li>Wife Id Card Copy</li><li>House Registration (Tabian ban)</li><li>Marriage Certificate</li><li>Six Months Bank Statement</li><li>Account Maintenance Certificate</li><li>Original Pakistani Passport (Old Passport is required if any)</li><li>Four Pictures</li><li>C.N.I.C Photo Copy</li><li>&nbsp;</li></ul><p>30 Days</p><h4>NON-ED Conference Visa</h4><p>Single Entry <strong>PKR 29500/-</strong>Per Person</p><p>REQUIREMENTS</p><ul><li>Six Months Bank Statement</li><li>Account Maintenance Certificate</li><li>N.T.N Number</li><li>Original Pakistani Passport (Old Passport is required if any)</li><li>Four Pictures</li><li>FRC Family Registration Certificate (if Applying with Family)</li><li>C.N.I.C Photo Copy</li><li>Invitation Letter from Thailand Company</li><li>Pakistani Company Employment Letter&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>90 Days</p><h4>Pakistani National On Non-B Visa</h4><p>Single Entry <strong>PKR 29500/-</strong>Per Person</p><p>REQUIREMENTS</p><ul><li>Passport first-page scan</li><li>Work permit scan</li><li>Valid Visa Scan</li><li>Invitation letter</li><li>Company Tax return</li><li>Company registration</li><li>DBDs Files</li><li>Bank Statement</li><li>Original Pakistani passport with previous passport</li><li>Pictures</li><li>C.N.I.C Photo Copy</li><li>Multiple Entry 1 Year 67000/- Per Person</li></ul><p>90 Days</p><h4>SINGLE/Double Transit Visa&nbsp;(TS-01/TS-02)</h4><p>Single Entry <strong>PKR 14500 /-</strong>Per Person</p><p>REQUIREMENTS</p><ul><li>Six Months Bank Statement</li><li>Account Maintenance Certificate</li><li>Business Covering Letter Pad&nbsp; &nbsp; OR Job Letter</li><li>N.T.N Number&nbsp; &nbsp; OR Last 3 Months Salary Slips</li><li>Onward Tickets&nbsp; &nbsp;Or Valid Visa of Other Country</li><li>Original Pakistani Passport (Old Passport is required if any)</li><li>Four Pictures</li><li>FRC Family Registration Certificate (if Applying with Family)</li><li>C.N.I.C Photo Copy</li><li>Double Transit&nbsp;&nbsp; 25500/-</li></ul><p>90 Days</p><h4>Study Visa</h4><p>Single Entry <strong>PKR 27500 /-</strong>Per Person</p><p>REQUIREMENTS</p><ul><li>Invitation letter from Thailand</li><li>Invitee, I\'d card</li><li>University registration</li><li>Degree photocopy from a Pakistani university</li><li>Bank Statement</li><li>Account maintenance</li><li>Source of income</li><li>Passport with the previous passport</li><li>Picture</li><li>CNIC photocopy</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>90 Days</p><h4>For Official Passport</h4><p>Single Entry <strong>PKR 11500 /-</strong>Per Person</p><p>REQUIREMENTS</p><ul><li>Note Verbal from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs</li><li>Department Letter (No Objection Certificate)</li><li>Original Pakistani Passport&nbsp;</li><li>Four Pictures</li><li>FRC Family Registration Certificate (if Applying with Family)</li><li>C.N.I.C Photo Copy</li></ul><h2>Thailand Visit Visa Requirements</h2><p>Thailand visit visa can vary based on the type of visa and your nationality. Here is a general overview of the requirements for a Tourist visa to Thailand:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Passport:</strong> A valid passport with at least six months of validity beyond the intended stay.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Visa Application Form:</strong> Complete the Thailand visa application form.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Passport Photos:</strong> Passport-sized photographs taken within the last six months.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Proof of Accommodation:</strong> Documentation showing your planned accommodation in Thailand, such as a hotel reservation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Financial Means: </strong>Proof of financial means, often in the form of recent bank statements, to demonstrate the ability to cover the expenses during your stay.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Round-Trip Flight Reservation:</strong> A confirmed round-trip flight reservation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Visa Fee:</strong> Payment of the applicable visa fee.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It\'s important to note that Thailand visa requirements may change, and additional documents or specific conditions might apply based on your nationality and the Thai embassy or consulate you are applying through.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Thailand Visit Visa Fee</h3><p>The Thailand visit visa fee can vary based on factors such as the type of visa, the applicant\'s nationality, and the duration of stay. Here are some general considerations:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tourist Visa (Single Entry) :</strong>The fee for a Tourist Visa (Single Entry) can be starting from 1,000 to 2,000 Thai Baht or more, depending on your nationality.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Multiple Entry Tourist Visa:</strong> If you are applying for a Multiple Entry Tourist Visa, the fee may be higher than that for a single-entry visa.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Visa on Arrival: </strong>The visa-on-arrival fee is typically payable in Thai Baht. The exact amount can vary but is usually starting from 2,000 Thai Baht.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Thailand Visit Visa Processing Time</h3><p>The processing time for a Thailand visit visa from Pakistan can vary depending on the type of visa, the embassy or consulate through which you apply, and the specific circumstances of your application.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here are some general considerations:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tourist Visa (Single Entry):</strong>The processing time for a Thailand Tourist Visa (Single Entry) is typically within a few working days. The exact duration can vary, and it\'s advisable to apply well in advance of your planned travel dates.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Visa on Arrival:&nbsp;</strong>For visa on arrival&nbsp;the process is generally quicker as it is completed upon arrival at the Thai immigration checkpoint. However, it\'s essential to have all required documents ready for a smooth entry process.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Multiple Entry Tourist Visa:</strong> The processing time for a multiple-entry tourist visa may be longer due to the additional features of the visa. It is advisable to apply well ahead of your intended travel dates.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Long-Stay Visa:</strong> Long-stay visas, such as those for extended periods, may require additional processing time due to the complexity of the application. It\'s recommended to check with the relevant embassy or consulate for specific details.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It\'s important to note that processing times can change, and factors such as the volume of applications and any unforeseen circumstances may affect the timeline.</p><h4>Thailand Visa On Arrival for Pakistan</h4><p>The citizens of Pakistan are eligible for Thailand\'s visa-on-arrival (VoA) program. Here are some key points regarding the Thailand visa on arrival for Pakistani citizens:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Eligibility:</strong> Pakistani citizens are eligible to apply for a Thailand visa on arrival when arriving at certain international airports and border checkpoints in Thailand.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Duration of Stay:</strong> The Visa on Arrival allows for a stay of up to 15 days in Thailand.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Documentation:</strong> Travelers must present a completed visa application form, a recent passport-sized photograph, proof of accommodation (hotel reservation), proof of financial means (starting from 10,000 Thai Baht per person or 20,000 Thai Baht per family), and a confirmed round-trip flight reservation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Visa Fee:</strong> The visa-on-arrival fee is payable in Thai Baht. It\'s recommended to carry the exact amount or check the official conversion rates.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Entry Points:</strong> Visa on Arrival can be obtained at international airports and designated land border checkpoints in Thailand.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Extension:</strong> It cannot be extended beyond the initial 15-day period.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Thailand Tourist Visa</h3><p>Thailand offers a tourist visa for visitors who wish to explore the country for tourism purposes. Below are some guidelines related to Thailand tourist visa for your help:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Eligibility:</strong> The tourist visa is generally available for individuals planning to visit Thailand for tourism purposes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Validity:</strong> The tourist visa is typically valid for a single entry, allowing the holder to stay in Thailand for a specific duration.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Duration of Stay:</strong> The duration of stay varies and is usually granted for up to 60 days. However, the actual duration can depend on the discretion of Thai immigration authorities.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Application Process:</strong> Travelers can apply for a tourist visa at the Royal Thai Embassy or Consulate in their home country. The application may involve completing a visa form, providing necessary documents, and paying the applicable visa fee.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Required Documents:</strong> Commonly required documents include a valid passport, completed visa application form, passport-sized photographs, proof of accommodation (hotel reservation), proof of financial means (bank statements), and a confirmed round-trip flight reservation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Visa Extension:</strong> In some cases, it may be possible to extend the tourist visa while in Thailand. Extensions are typically granted in 30-day increments, up to a maximum stay of 90 days.</p><h4>E visa Thailand</h4><p>Thailand has introduced an electronic visa (e-Visa) system for certain nationalities. However, specific details, eligibility criteria, and the list of eligible countries can change over time. Therefore, it\'s important to check before applying for Thailand\'s e-Visa program.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here are some general steps that are often associated with the e-visa application process:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Eligibility Check: </strong>Confirm if your nationality is eligible for the e-Visa program. Eligibility criteria can vary.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Visit the Official Website:</strong> Access the official website of the Thai e-Visa system or the Royal Thai Embassy/Consulate to initiate the application process.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Create an Account:</strong> Create an account on the e-Visa platform.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Complete the Application Form:</strong> Fill out the electronic visa application form with accurate and up-to-date information.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Upload Documents:</strong> Upload the required documents, which may include a copy of your passport, passport-sized photographs, proof of accommodation, and a flight itinerary.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Pay the Visa Fee:</strong> Pay the applicable visa fee using the available payment options.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submit the Application:</strong> Submit the completed application and wait for processing.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Receive e-Visa:</strong> If approved, you will receive the e-visa electronically. Ensure you have a printed copy or an electronic version for presentation upon arrival in Thailand.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>FAQs</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>How to apply Thailand visit visa from Pakistan?</h4><p>To apply for a Thailand visit visa from Pakistan, follow these steps:</p><ol><li>Visit the Thai embassy.</li><li>Fill out the Thailand visit visa application form with accurate and up-to-date information.</li><li>Prepare the required documents.</li><li>Submit the application.</li><li>Submit the completed application form and required documents.</li><li>Pay the applicable visa fee using the accepted payment methods.</li><li>Wait for the processing of your visa application. Once the visa is approved, collect it from the embassy or consulate. Some embassies may provide electronic visas that are sent via email.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>How to get a Thailand 90-day tourist visa?</h4><p>&nbsp;</p><p>To obtain a 90-day tourist stay in Thailand, apply for a standard Tourist Visa (Single Entry) from the Royal Thai Embassy. Once in Thailand, you may extend your stay by applying for additional 30-day extensions at the local Immigration Bureau, up to a maximum of 90 days from the initial entry.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Can I apply for Thailand visa online?</h4><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Yes, you can apply for Thailand visa online.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>How much is the Thailand visit visa fee for Pakistan?</h3><p>Thailand\'s visit visa fee for Pakistani citizens can vary based on the type of visa. For a standard Tourist Visa (Single Entry), the fee is starting from&nbsp; 2,000 Thai Baht.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>How long does it take to process a Thailand visit visa from Pakistan?</h3><p>The processing time for a Thailand visit visa from Pakistan is typically within a few working days. However, actual processing times may vary, and it\'s advisable to apply well in advance of your intended travel dates.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>What are Thailand\'s travel requirements for 2024?</h2><p>Thailand\'s travel requirements can vary based on the purpose and duration of the visit. Typically, visitors need a valid passport, and a visa if applicable, and may be subject to health and COVID-19-related protocols.</p><h2>Is there travel insurance for visitors to Thailand?</h2><p>Yes, travel insurance for visitors to Thailand is highly recommended. It provides coverage for medical emergencies, trip cancellations, and other unexpected events. Many insurance companies offer specific plans tailored to the needs of international travelers visiting Thailand.</p><h2>&nbsp;</h2><p>&nbsp;</p><h4><br>&nbsp;</h4>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:29:34','2024-02-26 20:46:21'),(1382,4,'Malaysia visit visa | Malaysia visa | Malaysia e visa','Malaysia tourist visa, Malaysia visa for Pakistani, Malaysia visa requirements, Malaysia visa price & Malaysia visa online by rehmantravel.com','','visa/malaysia-visa','Malaysia Visit Visa',NULL,'Malaysia.webp','Visa','USD','55',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,'',0,1,'<h2>Malaysia Visit Visa</h2><p>Rehman Travels is your trusted partner for all your travel needs. Our Malaysia visits visa services are designed to make your journey to this captivating destination smooth, convenient, and hassle-free. Whether you\'re traveling for leisure, business, or visiting friends and family, we\'re here to assist you every step of the way.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Our expert team of visa consultants provides comprehensive guidance and assessment to determine the most suitable visa category for your travel needs. We evaluate your eligibility criteria, and documentation requirements, and ensure compliance with Malaysian immigration regulations.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Contact us today to explore our Malaysia visit visa services and take the first step towards an unforgettable travel experience.</p><h2>Malaysia E Visa</h2><p>The Malaysia e-Visa is an electronic travel authorization that allows eligible travelers to enter Malaysia for tourism, business, or visiting purposes. This hassle-free visa option streamlines the application process, enabling travelers to obtain their visas online without the need for physical documentation or embassy visits.</p><h3>How to Apply for the Malaysia E-Visa?</h3><p><strong>Check Eligibility:</strong> Ensure that you are a citizen of a country eligible for the Malaysia e-Visa program. Refer to the official website for the list of eligible nationalities.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Online Application:</strong> Complete the online application form available on the official Malaysia e-Visa portal. Provide accurate information and upload the required documents as per the instructions.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Payment:</strong> Pay the e-Visa processing fee using a valid credit or debit card. The fee may vary depending on the duration and type of visa selected.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Application Processing:</strong> Once submitted, the Malaysian immigration authorities will process your e-Visa application. You can track the status of your application online using the provided reference number.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Visa Approval:</strong> Upon approval, you will receive your e-visa via email. Print a copy of the e-Visa document and carry it with you during your travels to Malaysia.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Entry into Malaysia:</strong> Present your printed e-visa document along with your passport to the immigration officers upon arrival in Malaysia. Ensure that your passport is valid for at least six months from entry.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Discover the enchanting landscapes, vibrant cultures, and warm hospitality of Malaysia with the convenience of the e-Visa program. Say goodbye to lengthy visa procedures and embrace the simplicity of online visa applications with Rehman Travels.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Malaysia Tourist Visa</h3><p>If you\'re planning to explore the wonders of Malaysia for tourism purposes, the Malaysia Tourist Visa is your key to unlocking unforgettable experiences in this enchanting destination.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>What is a Malaysia Tourist Visa</strong>?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The Malaysia tourist visa is a travel authorization issued by the Malaysian government to individuals intending to visit Malaysia for leisure, sightseeing, and recreational activities. Whether you\'re drawn to the bustling streets of Kuala Lumpur, the pristine beaches of Langkawi, or the lush rainforests of Borneo, the tourist visa allows you to immerse yourself in the diverse beauty and charm of Malaysia.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Key Features of the Malaysia Tourist Visa</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Duration of Stay:</strong> The tourist visa typically allows for stays of up to 30 or 90 days, depending on your nationality and the specific visa conditions.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Single or Multiple Entry:</strong> Depending on your travel plans and visa type, you may be eligible for either single or multiple entries during the visa validity period.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Validity Period:</strong> The Malaysia tourist visa is typically valid for a specified period, allowing you to plan your travel dates accordingly.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Eligibility Criteria:</strong> The eligibility criteria for the tourist visa vary based on your nationality, intended duration of stay, and compliance with Malaysian immigration regulations.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>Malaysia Visit Visa Requirements</h3><p>The requirements for a Malaysia visit visa may vary depending on your nationality and the specific purpose of your visit. However, generally, the following are the common requirements for obtaining a Malaysia visit visa:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Completed Visa Application Form:</strong> You will need to fill out the Malaysia visit visa application form accurately and truthfully. This form can usually be obtained from the Malaysian embassy or consulate in your country or downloaded from their official website.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Passport:</strong> Your passport must be valid for at least six months beyond your intended stay in Malaysia. It should also have at least one blank page for visa stamping.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Passport-sized Photographs:</strong> Provide recent passport-sized photographs meeting the specifications set by the Malaysian authorities. Usually, the photographs should be in color, with a white background.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Proof of Travel Itinerary: </strong>Provide details of your travel itinerary, including flight reservations, accommodation bookings, and planned activities during your stay in Malaysia.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Proof of Sufficient Funds:</strong> You may need to demonstrate that you have sufficient funds to cover your expenses during your stay in Malaysia. This could include bank statements, traveler\'s checks, or a letter of sponsorship if applicable.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Proof of Accommodation:</strong> Provide evidence of where you will be staying during your visit to Malaysia. This could be hotel reservations, a letter of invitation from a host, or other relevant documentation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Travel Insurance:</strong> While not always mandatory, having travel insurance that covers medical emergencies, repatriation, and other unforeseen circumstances is highly recommended.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Additional Documents:</strong> Depending on your specific circumstances and the purpose of your visit, you may be required to provide additional documents such as a letter of invitation, proof of employment or enrollment in a study program, and other relevant supporting materials.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Malaysia Visit Visa Processing Time</h4><p>The processing time for a Malaysia visit visa can vary depending on several factors, including the type of visa, the volume of visa applications being processed at the time, and the efficiency of the processing center. However, here are some general guidelines regarding the processing time for Malaysia Visit Visas:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Normal Processing Time:</strong> In general, the normal processing time for a Malaysia visit visa ranges from 5 to 10 working days from the date of submission of the visa application. This timeframe may vary depending on the specific embassy or consulate where the application is lodged.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Expedited Processing:</strong> Some Malaysian embassies or consulates may offer expedited or express processing services for an additional fee. Expedited processing typically shortens the processing time to 1 to 3 working days, but this option may only be available at some visa processing centers.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Peak Seasons and Holidays:</strong> During peak travel seasons or holidays, such as school holidays or festive seasons, visa processing times may be longer due to the higher volume of visa applications being received.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Incomplete or Inaccurate Applications:</strong> Delays in visa processing can occur if the visa application is incomplete or if any required documentation is missing or inaccurate. It\'s essential to ensure that all required documents are submitted correctly to avoid processing delays.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Additional Processing Requirements:</strong> In some cases, additional processing requirements such as background checks or further documentation may be necessary, which can extend the processing time beyond the standard timeframe.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Type of Visa:</strong> The processing time may also vary depending on the type of Malaysia visit visa being applied for, such as a single-entry visa, multiple-entry visa, or transit visa.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Malaysia Visit Visa Apply</h4><p>To apply for a Malaysia visit visa, you will typically need to follow these general steps:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Determine the Type of Visa You Need:</strong> Depending on the purpose of your visit to Malaysia (tourism, business, visiting family or friends, etc.), you\'ll need to determine the appropriate type of visit visa you need.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Check Visa Requirements:</strong> Visit the official website of the Malaysian embassy or consulate in your country or the website of the Malaysian Immigration Department to check the specific requirements for the type of visit visa you are applying for. Make sure you have all the necessary documents and information ready before starting the application process.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Complete the Application Form:</strong> Obtain the Malaysia visit visa application form from the Malaysian embassy or consulate in your country, or download it from their official website. Fill out the application form accurately and completely, following the instructions provided.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Gather Required Documents:</strong> Collect all the required supporting documents for your visa application, including your passport, passport-size photographs, proof of travel itinerary, proof of sufficient funds, proof of accommodation, travel insurance (if required), and any other relevant documents specified by the Malaysian authorities.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submit Your Application:</strong> Submit your completed visa application form along with the required documents to the nearest Malaysian embassy, consulate, or authorized visa processing center in your country. Make sure to pay any applicable visa processing fees as per the instructions provided.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Attend Visa Interview (if required):</strong> Some applicants may be required to attend a visa interview as part of the application process. If an interview is required, prepare for it by familiarizing yourself with your travel plans and providing truthful responses to any questions asked.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Wait for Visa Processing:</strong> Once your visa application is submitted, await processing by the Malaysian immigration authorities. Processing times may vary depending on the volume of applications and other factors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Receive Visa Approval:</strong> Upon approval, your Malaysia visit visa will be stamped or affixed to your passport, permitting you to enter Malaysia for the specified duration and purpose of travel.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Plan Your Travel:</strong> Once you receive your approved visa, make travel arrangements and plan your itinerary for your visit to Malaysia. Ensure you comply with all visa conditions and entry requirements upon arrival in Malaysia.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It\'s essential to follow the specific instructions and guidelines provided by the Malaysian embassy or consulate in your country and to apply for your Malaysia visit visa well in advance of your intended travel dates to allow for sufficient processing time.</p><h3>&nbsp;</h3><p>FAQs</p><h4>What is the cost of a Malaysia 1 year visa from Pakistan?</h4><p>The cost for a one-year Malaysia visa single or multiple entry is 449 RM.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>What is the validity period of a Malaysia e-visa for tourism?</h4><p>It is normally valid for a Single Entry and for a period not exceeding three (3) months from the date of issuance.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Can I apply for a tourist visa online for Malaysia, and if so, what are the required documents?</h4><p>Yes, you can apply for a tourist visa online for Malaysia through the e-Visa system. Here are the general documents required when applying for a Malaysia e-Visa for tourism:</p><ul><li>A valid passport</li><li>Recent passport-sized photograph(s)</li><li>Details of your travel plans, including flight reservations, accommodation bookings, and planned activities in Malaysia.</li><li>Evidence of sufficient funds to cover your expenses during your stay in Malaysia.</li><li>Documentation showing where you will be staying during your visit to Malaysia.</li><li>Travel Insurance</li></ul><h4>Are there any specific eligibility criteria for obtaining a Malaysian tourist visa?</h4><p>Yes, there are specific eligibility criteria that individuals must meet to obtain a Malaysian tourist visa, which include:</p><ul><li>Valid passport</li><li>Applicants must demonstrate that their visit to Malaysia is for tourism purposes.</li><li>Sufficient funds</li><li>Applicants may be required to provide proof of onward or return travel arrangements.</li><li>No intention to work</li><li>Applicants must comply with the immigration laws and regulations of Malaysia.</li><li>Applicants should be in good health and have no criminal record or history of immigration violations.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>How long does it typically take to process a Malaysia visit visa application?</h4><p>Processing times can indeed vary based on the type of visa and the method of application. If you apply for a Malaysia visa through eNTRI, the visa should be processed within 48 to 72 hours (2 to 3 days). Plus, if you apply for a Malaysia visa manually, the processing time may vary depending on the office handling your application. However, in most cases, the Malaysia visa is processed within 7-8 working days.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>What is the maximum duration of stay allowed on a Malaysia tourist visa?</h4><p>The maximum duration of stay allowed on a Malaysia tourist visa is typically up to 30 days from the date of entry for most tourists.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Can I extend my stay in Malaysia on a tourist visa, and what is the process for an extension?</h4><p>Yes, tourists can extend their stay in Malaysia on a tourist visa through the Immigration Department of Malaysia. The process involves submitting an application for a visa extension at least seven days before the current visa expires, providing relevant documents, and paying the necessary fees.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Are there any restrictions on the activities allowed while on a Malaysian tourist visa?</h4><p>While on a Malaysia tourist visa, individuals are typically restricted from engaging in activities such as employment, business operations, or other forms of paid work. However, tourists are allowed to participate in tourism-related activities, sightseeing, recreational pursuits, and cultural experiences within the country. It\'s important to adhere to the conditions specified by the Malaysian immigration authorities and refrain from activities prohibited by the terms of the tourist visa.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>What are the financial requirements for obtaining a Malaysia visit visa?</h4><p>The financial requirements for obtaining a Malaysia visit visa typically involve demonstrating sufficient funds to cover expenses during the stay, including accommodation, transportation, meals, and other expenses, supported by bank statements or financial documents.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Is travel insurance mandatory for a Malaysia tourist visa application?</h4><p>Travel insurance is not typically mandatory for a Malaysia tourist visa application, but it is highly recommended to have coverage for medical emergencies and other unforeseen events during your stay in Malaysia.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Can I apply for a multiple-entry visa for Malaysia for future visits?</h4><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Yes, you can apply for a multiple-entry visa for Malaysia, allowing for future visits within the visa\'s validity period, typically up to 1 year, depending on eligibility and purpose of travel.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>What is the procedure for obtaining a visa for family members traveling with me to Malaysia?</h4><p>To obtain a visa for family members traveling with you to Malaysia, submit their visa applications along with yours, provide required documents such as passports, application forms, and supporting documentation, and pay applicable fees through the designated channels or application centers. Family members may include spouses, children, parents, or other dependents, and eligibility criteria may vary based on the type of visa and relationship.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Are there any specific health requirements or vaccinations needed for a Malaysian tourist visa?</h4><p>There are no specific health requirements or vaccinations needed for a Malaysia tourist visa, but it\'s advisable to be up-to-date on routine vaccinations and consider health advisories for the region you plan to visit.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Can I apply for a visa on arrival, or is it mandatory to obtain one in advance?</h4><p>Yes, individuals planning to enter Malaysia for tourism purposes and who fall under the Malaysian visa regime will need to obtain a tourist visa before they arrive in the country.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>Are there any age restrictions for individuals applying for a Malaysia tourist visa?</h4><p>&nbsp;</p><p>There are generally no specific age restrictions for individuals applying for a Malaysia tourist visa.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>What is the visa fee for a Malaysia tourist visa, and are there any additional charges?</h4><p>The visa fee for a Malaysia tourist visa can vary depending on the type of visa, the duration of stay, and the applicant\'s nationality. The visa fee for a Malaysia tourist visa typically ranges from $20 to $50 for a single-entry visa, while multiple-entry visas may cost more.</p>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:29:34','2024-03-29 10:52:03'),(1383,4,'Azerbaijan Visit visa | Azerbaijan visa | Azerbaijan e visa','Azerbaijan tourist visa, Azerbaijan visa from Pakistan, Azerbaijan online visa, Azerbaijan visit visa fee for Pakistani, Azerbaijan visit visa consultancy','https://www.rehmantravel.com/visa/azerbaijan-visa/','visa/azerbaijan-visa','Azerbaijan Visit Visa',NULL,NULL,'Visa','USD','0.00',6,'<h1><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Azerbaijan Visit Visa</span></span></h1>','','','',0,0,'<p>Azerbaijan officially the Republic of Azerbaijan is the largest country in Caucasus. Azerbaijan handicrafts like carpets, metal work, shabaka, and khatem karlyg are very