ing in the UK can be a dream come true for individuals seeking to advance their careers or explore new horizons. However, to work legally in the UK as a foreign national, obtaining a UK Work Permit is an essential step in the process. </span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">What is a UK Work Permit?</span></strong> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">A UK Work Permit, also known as a Tier 2 (General) Visa, is a type of visa that allows foreign nationals to work in the United Kingdom. This visa is specifically designed for skilled workers and is part of the Points-Based System (PBS), which assesses applicants based on various criteria.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Who Needs a UK Work Permit?</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Some people who wish to work in the UK require a Work Permit. Whether you need one depends on your nationality and the type of work you intend to do. Here&#39;s a breakdown:</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Non-European Economic Area (EEA) and non-Swiss nationals:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">If you are a citizen of a country outside the EEA and Switzerland, you will generally need a UK Work Permit to work legally in the UK.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>EEA and Swiss nationals:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">EEA and Swiss nationals could work in the UK without a Work Permit due to the freedom of movement within the European Union. However, this policy may have changed, so it&#39;s essential to check the latest immigration regulations.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">. </span></p>\n\n<h2>UK Work Permit Visa Requirements</h2>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The UK Work Permit, also known as the Tier 2 (General) Visa, had specific requirements that applicants needed to meet to be eligible. However, immigration policies and requirements can change, so it&#39;s essential to check the latest information on the official UK government website or consult an immigration expert for the most up-to-date requirements. </span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Here are the typical requirements for a UK Work Permit: </span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Job Offer from a UK Employer: :</strong> You must have a valid job offer from a UK employer with a Tier 2 Sponsor License. The employer will provide you with a Certificate of Sponsorship (COS), which you must include in your visa application.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>Appropriate Skill Level: </strong>Your job must be at an appropriate skill level, typically at or above RQF Level 6 (National Qualifications Framework).</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Salary Requirement:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">You must meet the minimum salary requirement for your specific job. The salary threshold may vary depending on your occupation and job</span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">requirements.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><strong>English Language Proficiency: </strong> You may need to prove your knowledge of the English language, usually by passing an approved English language test. However, exemptions may apply if you are a national of an English-speaking country or have a degree taught in English.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Salary Requirement: </strong></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">You must meet the minimum salary requirement for your specific job. The salary threshold may vary depending on your occupation and job requirements</span>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Maintenance Funds: </strong></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">You should show that you have enough money to support yourself without recourse to public funds during your stay in the UK.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Tuberculosis Test:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Depending on your country of residence, you may need to undergo a tuberculosis (TB) test as part of the application process.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Biometric Information:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">You will be required to provide biometric information, including fingerprints and a photograph, as part of the application process.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Criminal Record Certificate:<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"> </span></strong></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">In some cases, you may need to provide a criminal record certificate from your home country or any country where you have lived for more than 12 months over the last ten years.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Healthcare Surcharge:</span></strong> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">You may be required to pay the Immigration Health and Social Care Surcharge (IHS) as part of your application. This surcharge gives you access to the National Health Service (NHS) during your stay in the UK.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Other Documents:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Depending on your specific circumstances, you may need to provide other documents or information to support your application.</span></p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">How to Apply for a UK Work Permit?</span></h3>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The application process for a UK Work Permit can be complex, but with careful preparation, it&#39;s manageable. Here&#39;s a step-by-step guide:</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Find a job offer:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">First and foremost, you need a job offer from a UK employer with a valid Tier 2 Sponsor License. Your prospective employer will issue you a Certificate of Sponsorship (COS), which you will need for your application.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Check eligibility:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Ensure you meet all the eligibility criteria, including minimum salary requirements, English language proficiency, and maintenance funds. Different criteria apply to various categories of Tier 2 visas.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Complete the online application:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Submit your application online through the UK government&#39;s official website. You will need to provide personal details, biometric information, and details about your job offer.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Biometric appointment:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">You must attend a biometric appointment at a UK Visa Application Center in your home country to provide fingerprints and photographs.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Attend an interview (if required):</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">In some cases, you may be asked to attend an interview as part of the application process.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Wait for a decision: </strong></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The processing time for a UK Work Permit application can vary, so it&#39;s essential to apply well in advance of your planned start date.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Visa issuance:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">If your application is successful, you will receive a visa vignette in your passport, allowing you to enter the UK. Upon arrival, you will collect your Biometric Residence Permit (BRP) within ten days.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">UK Work Permit Visa Fees</span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The fees for a UK Work Permit, specifically the Tier 2 (General) Visa, varied depending on the length of stay, the type of application, and whether you were applying from inside or outside the UK. </span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Please remember that immigration fees are subject to change, so checking the latest fee schedule on the official UK government website or with the nearest UK Visa Application Center is essential. </span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Here is a general overview of the fees: </span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Tier 2 (General) Visa from Outside the UK</strong></span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">For a visa that is valid for up to 3 years: &pound;610</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">For a visa that is valid for more than 3 years: &pound;1,220</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Tier 2 (General) Visa Extension from Inside the UK</strong></span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">For a visa extension for up to 3 years: &pound;704</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">For a visa extension for more than 3 years: &pound;1,408</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Priority Processing (Optional):</strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"> </span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">If you want your application to be processed more quickly, you can opt for priority or super-priority services at an additional cost. The fees for these services can change and will depend on your applicable location. The fees were approximately &pound;220 for priority processing and &pound;956 for super-priority processing.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Dependents:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">If you are applying with family members (dependents), additional fees for each dependent are included in the application.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Healthcare Surcharge:</strong></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"> In addition to the visa application fee, you may also be required to pay the Immigration Health and Social Care Surcharge (IHS) as part of your application. The IHS fee varies depending on the length of your visa and is calculated based on the years you intend to stay in the UK.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Other Optional Services:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Additional optional services, such as the document translation service or courier return of your documents, may have separate fees.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Please note that these fees are subject to change, and the UK government may update its fee schedule periodically. Therefore, verify the current fees and payment methods before applying. Additionally, it&#39;s recommended to ensure that you have the correct fee amount in the correct currency at the time of application, as the payment process may vary depending on your location.</span></p>\n\n<h5><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">What to Expect After Receiving Your UK Work Permit?</span></span></h5>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Once you have your UK Work Permit and arrive in the UK, there are several key points to keep in mind:</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Length of stay:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Your Tier 2 (General) Visa typically allows you to work in the UK for up to five years and 14 days, or the time specified on your Certificate of Sponsorship, whichever is shorter. You may be eligible to extend your visa or apply for permanent residency (Indefinite Leave to Remain) after a certain period</span>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Change of employment:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">If you change jobs or employers while on a Tier 2 Visa, you must inform the Home Office and ensure your new employer holds a valid Tier 2 Sponsor License.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Family members: </strong></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Your spouse, civil partner, or dependent children may be eligible to join you in the UK under certain circumstances.</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Taxes and healthcare:</strong></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">As a UK worker, you will be subject to UK tax laws and may be eligible for access to the National Health Service (NHS).</span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h6><span style=\"color:#0000FF;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Conclusion</span></span></h6>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Obtaining a UK Work Permit is a significant step toward realizing your professional aspirations in the United Kingdom. While the process can be intricate, thorough research and preparation can help you navigate it successfully. </span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Keep in mind that immigration policies can change, so it&#39;s crucial to consult the latest guidance from the UK government or seek advice from immigration experts before initiating your application. With determination and the right approach, your journey to working in the UK can become a reality, opening doors to opportunities and personal growth. </span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">You can also consult Rehman Travels for the UK work permit visa. It&#39;s essential to make informed decisions and seek assistance from reliable and trustworthy sources when dealing with immigration matters, as the outcome can significantly impact your future in the UK. </span></p>\n</div>\n',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:29:34',NULL),(1398,4,'Saudi Arabia Visa | Saudi Arabia e visa | Saudi Arabia visa online | Saudi Arabia one year Visit Vis','apply Saudi Arabia one year visit visa online, e  visit visa Saudi Arabia one year, Saudi Arabia one year visit visa price, Saudi Arabia one year visit visa requirements, Saudi Arabia one year Visit Visa process, umrah visa services, cheap umrah visa, at rehmantravel.com','https://www.rehmantravel.com/visa/saudi-arabia-one-year-multiple-personal-visit-visa','visa/saudi-arabia-one-year-multiple-personal-visit-visa','Saudi Arabia Visit Visa',NULL,'Thailand.jpg','Visa','USD','0.00',20,NULL,'','','',0,0,'<div class=\"ramadan-packages print-hajj-packages\">\n<h1 class=\"title\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/ckeditor_images/images/Saudi%20Arabia%20Multiple%20Personal%20Visit%20Visa.jpeg\" style=\"width: 100%;\" /></h1>\n</div>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:29:34','2024-02-22 02:48:33'),(1399,4,'Kazakhstan visit visa | Kazakhstan visa | Kazakhstan e visa','Kazakhstan tourist visa, Kazakhstan visa for Pakistani, Kazakhstan visa requirements, Kazakhstan visa price & Kazakhstan visa online by rehmantravel.com','https://www.rehmantravel.com/visa/kazakhstan-visit-visa','visa/kazakhstan-visit-visa','Kazakhstan Visit Visa',NULL,NULL,'Visa','USD','0.00',10,NULL,'','','',0,0,'<p>While Kazakhstan has beautiful steppe and mountain scenery, there are no yurts like in Kyrgyzstan or Mongolia. Kazakhstan has interesting medieval Islamic architecture, but Uzbekistan has more.</p><p>Add to that the sheer size of Kazakhstan, few tourism companies and restrictive government policies (it’s getting better): more limiting factors in attracting tourists.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>So why still visit Kazakhstan?</strong></p><p>Kazakhstan appeals to different people in different ways. Chinese travelers enjoy the fresh air (outside of the cities) and the lack of people, while Arabian visitors love how it is so green, and kind of Muslim, but not too much. Snow-white, ice-cold winters attract visitors from tropical countries.</p><p>For Westerners, the main selling point are Kazakhstan’s&nbsp;unique landscapes, dripping with freedom. On top of that, singular experiences include the Baikonur Cosmodrome, the <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/semey/kurchatov-polygon/\">Semipalatinsk Atomic Test Site</a>, the landscapes of Mangystau, the balbal of the steppe, glitzy Astana and chaste <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/altai/\">Altai</a>.</p><p>If history and politics are your main interests, Kazakhstan is fascinating as the country with the largest Soviet legacy, due to forced population transfers, massive industrialization and subsequent ghost towns, space launches and atomic bomb tests, gulags and banished Russian intellectuals like Dostoyevski, Solzhenitsyn, Eisenstein and Trotsky.</p><p>Table of Contents</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#where-to-go\">Where to go?</a><ul><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#first-stop\">First stop</a></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#off-the-beaten-track\">Off the beaten track</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#transport\">Transport</a><ul><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#trains-planes-buses\">Trains, planes &amp; buses</a></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#self-driving-cycling\">Self-driving &amp; cycling</a></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#winter-travel\">Winter travel</a></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#cross-border-transport\">Cross-border transport</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#practical-details\">Practical details</a><ul><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#when-to-go\">When to go</a></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#basics\">Basics</a></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#budget-and-accommodation\">Budget and accommodation</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#tours-and-tour-operators\">Tours and tour operators</a></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#more-country-guides\">More country guides</a></li><li><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/#more-on-kazakhstan\">More on Kazakhstan</a></li></ul><h2>Where to go?</h2><p>We understand that many people want easy, bite-sized advice from a travel guide. <i>Gimme 5 highlights and a 2-week itinerary and let me get on with my life.</i> We get that. But Kazakhstan defies any attempt at pigeonholing; on top of that, most visits are part of an overland itinerary, so it all depends on where you’re coming from and heading towards.</p><p>Have a look at our list of<a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/things-to-do/\"> 40 great things to do in Kazakhstan</a> to get your creative trip-planning juices flowing.</p><h3>&nbsp;</h3><p>For the majority of visitors, <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/almaty-region/\">Almaty region</a> and the <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/south/\">southern area around Shymkent</a> are the only things they will see of Kazakhstan. There is nothing wrong with that. Kazakhstan is a very big country: in area, these 2 regions put together are bigger than the whole of Italy or Japan.</p><p>Together, they provide a great sample of what Kazakhstan is all about, both culturally, historically and in terms of natural beauty. Since they border <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/uzbekistan/\">Uzbekistan</a>, <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kyrgyzstan/\">Kyrgyzstan</a> and China, visiting <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/south/\">the south</a> and the <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/almaty-region/\">Almaty region</a> makes a lot of sense in many a overland itinerary.</p><p>If you only get to see 1 place: <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/almaty-region/\">Almaty region</a> has the most attractions and the best infrastructure. 5 national parks offer deserts, steppe, wildlife and high mountains, as well as history stretching back thousands of years, all surrounding Central Asia’s most buzzing city, <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/almaty/\">Almaty</a>.</p><h3>Off the beaten track</h3><p>Only those who like to go further off the beaten track (preferably with their own transport or a budget for tours) will want to venture into the other regions of Kazakhstan. If you have a specific interest like history, archaeology, botany or birding, you will also find much to enjoy here.</p><p><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/\">In the North</a>, Kazakhstan’s brash new capital Astana stands in stark contrast to&nbsp;the modest <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/altai/\">Altai mountains</a>. <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/semey/\">Semey</a> surprises with its museums and history, and serves as the gateway to the <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/semey/kurchatov-polygon/\">Semipalatinsk Test Site</a>. Other northern cities like <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/oskemen/\">Oskemen</a>, <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/petropavl/\">Petropavl</a>, <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/pavlodar/\">Pavlodar</a>, <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/altai/ridder/\">Ridder</a> and <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/north/ekibastuz/\">Ekibastuz</a> are trying to acquire a life of their own after being willed into existence by the Soviet state to build up its industrial base.</p><p><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/west/\">In the West</a>, the oil towns of Atyrau and Aqtau border the Caspian Sea, but tourists come instead for its hinterland of stark desert landscapes like the Ustyurt plateau, which hides underground mosques like the sanctuary of <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/west/beket-ata/\">Beket-Ata</a>. Separated by an enormous expanse of steppeland dubbed by one traveler as “the most boring place on Earth”, in the northwest, visitors to historic <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/west/uralsk/\">Uralsk</a> and boomtown <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/center/aktobe/\">Aqtobe</a> are few and far between.</p><p><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/center/\">In the Center</a>, the steppe gets even bigger and more desolate. Remote steppe oddities of niche interest are Kazakhstan’s spiritual heartland at Ulytau, <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/center/kyzylorda/aralsk/\">Aralsk and the zombie Aral Sea</a> and space port Baikonur. Main cities are progressive <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/center/karaganda/\">Karaganda</a> and keeper of Kazakh traditions <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/kazakhstan/center/kyzylorda/\">Kyzylorda</a>.</p><h2>Transport</h2><h3>Trains, planes &amp; buses</h3><p>Kazakhstan is developing its <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/transport/train/kazakhstan/\">rail network</a>, and several high-speed trains now connect the major cities. Other trains are still slow,&nbsp;their speed reflected by&nbsp;their&nbsp;low prices.</p><p>Flights are more expensive, although low-cost airlines now exist in Kazakhstan: FlyArystan, SCAT and Qazaq Air.</p><p>For travelers who have the time, the train is a comfortable and budget-friendly alternative to the airplane. For those who don’t, the airplane is the quickest way to get around Kazakhstan with airfields in all corners of the country.</p><p><i>Rolling through Kazakhstan…</i></p><p>Buses and shared taxis are usually the&nbsp;only way to get to smaller destinations. Less comfortable and more dangerous, we do not recommend taking them for long distances. Like train stations, city bus stations are a good place to store your luggage for the day if you are planning a stop-over.</p><p>Within cities, <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/transport/taxi-apps/\">ride-hailing and taxi apps</a> are available.</p><h3>Self-driving &amp; cycling</h3><p><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/transport/driving/kazakhstan/\">Driving Kazakhstan</a> is perhaps the best way to experience this huge country, since many of its attractions are difficult to reach on public transport. It’s the perfect way to experience the freedom of Kazakhstan’s great outdoors. <a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/car-rental/\">Car rentals</a> have become more affordable in recent years, in case you did not bring your own wheels.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><i>Eagles flying overhead at Lake Markakol, a 7-hour drive from Oskemen</i></p><p><a href=\"https://caravanistan.com/transport/cycling/kazakhstan/\">Cycling Kazakhstan</a> – there are some nice routes available, especially in the eastern corners, in combination with Kyrgyzstan and Mongolia. Cycling in the rest of the country is a real challenge.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>',1,163,'agent','2024-02-21 01:29:34','2024-02-26 20:51:55'),(1400,7,'franchise meta title','franchise meta title','franchise-reg','franchise-reg','Franchise Registration',NULL,NULL,NULL,'USD','0.00',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,'<p>Franchise is a type of license or a form of business where a franchisee is allowed to use the product, and services and operate a business based on the franchiser (owner of the product) business concept using its trademark. Rehman Travels is a prominent name in the travel and tourism industry of Pakistan. We offer the golden opportunity by setting up a network of the franchises across the country. Rehman Travels (franchisor) assist you in establishing your own business and becoming a partner with the most renowned travel management company.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4><strong>Franchisee Benefits</strong></h4><ul><li>Associate with leading holiday brands and operate a profit-generating business.</li><li>Travel deals and discounts will be shared with the franchisee</li><li>The risk of business failure is reduced by being part of a trusted company</li><li>5% commission on booking of World tour, Pakistan tour, Umrah tour, and Hajj tour.</li><li>We will promote your business on our website and social networking sites (Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn) which is totally free for you.</li><li>We will boost your business by diverting the client of your area/sector directly to you</li><li>Regular staff training for effective functioning.</li><li>Opportunity to sell a wide range of travel services like domestic and international air tickets, domestic and international holidays, Umrah tours, visa processing, and many more travel-related services.</li><li>&nbsp;</li></ul><h4><strong>Franchise Requirements</strong></h4><ul><li>The franchisee should be a DTS (Department of Tourist Services) license holder.</li><li>Provide the bank statement for the last six months.</li><li>Minimum 2 years agreement with Rehman Travels.</li><li>The franchisee should deposit PKR 500,000 as the refundable security deposit.</li><li>Use our name on your website and billboards.</li><li>The design of the billboard is provided by Rehman Travels.</li><li>Only market/sell Rehman Travel products not any other.</li><li>You are responsible for all rental, taxes, and losses of your franchise.</li><li>If you have any of your own or any third-party products/properties then a separate agreement shall be made with the head office.</li><li>Rehman Travels is not responsible for any of your financial dealings or liabilities.</li><li>You will have to make advance payments for all your airline ticket purchases with Rehman Travels.</li><li>Open franchise in Lahore, Karachi, and Peshawar but not in Islamabad.</li><li>&nbsp;</li></ul><h4><strong>Services of Rehman Travels</strong></h4><ul><li>With more than 400 IATA Airlines tickets and 20,000 flight connections and routes you can search in less than 3 seconds</li><li>Provide the SOTO (Sold Out Travel Out) service</li><li>Travel Insurance and Visa Consultancy</li><li>Provide different modes of transport to rent a car for business executives and VIP dignitaries which includes</li><li>Facilitate customers with the protocol.</li><li>Provide special meals (breakfast, lunch, and dinner)</li><li>Deal with World tour, Pakistan tour, Umrah tour, and Hajj tour</li><li>Provide the AirMiles exchange benefit.</li><li>&nbsp;</li></ul><h4><strong>Termination conditions</strong></h4><ul><li>Your franchise can be terminated from Rehman Travels in case you are found to be misusing our name, or doing any illegal activities, or involved in any financial irregularities with any person or companies.</li><li>You can end the business after settling all of your business liabilities towards the Franchisor.</li><li>&nbsp;</li></ul><h4><strong>Register a Franchise with Rehman Travels</strong></h4><ul><li>For the registration, you can simply fill out the form and register yourself.</li><li>&nbsp;</li></ul><h4><strong>Help Line</strong></h4><p><strong>Email:</strong> helpdesk@rehmantravel.com</p>',1,156,'agent','2024-03-08 06:37:09',NULL),(1401,12,'Soon Valley - Uchali Lake - Khabeki Lake Tour Packages - Rehman Travel','Soon valley is a hidden treasure of salt range with its natural attractions and particularly for its vast lakes,  worldwide tourist regularly visit soon valley and enjoy beautiful birdsong and clean shining flowing water of soon valley lake or Lake Uchhal','pakistan/punjab/adventures/bird-watching','pakistan/punjab/adventures/bird-watching','Bird Watching',NULL,NULL,'Domestic Tour','USD','0',20,'','<p>&nbsp;</p>  <h4>Price Includes</h4>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <ol style=\"list-style: decimal; padding-left: 20px;\"> 	<li>Private air conditioned transport</li> 	<li>Accommodation in tents for 1 nights</li> 	<li>Dinner and breakfast</li> 	<li>Guide for complete tour</li> 	<li>Basic First Aid kit<br /> 	&n