ad is situated a few kilometres from Kohala Bridge which forms the entry point into Azad Kashmir from this side of the border. We shall visit the ruins of Red fort. We shall visit the Domail view point which is the confluence of Jhelum and Neelum Rivers. From Muzaffarabad we drive to Keran along the Neelum River. Further along the Neelum River we drive to Sharda to see an old Buddhist monastery. From here we go on to Arang Kel which is situated at 8,379feet/2554meters and has a military post and the village across the river on the Indian side is also called Kel. The last destination would be Taobat which is the point where Neelum River enters our territory from Indian side. &nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n',0,163,'agent','2024-03-14 21:42:12','2024-03-18 04:31:22'),(1412,12,'Indus Civilization','Indus Civilization','pakistantours/indus-civilization','pakistantours/indus-civilization','Indus Civilization',NULL,NULL,'Domestic Tour','USD','0',20,'','<p>&nbsp;</p>  <h4><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><...','<p>&nbsp;</p>  <h4><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><...',NULL,0,0,'<p>Pakistan has the traces of the oldest civilizations of the world and from Mehargarh to&nbsp;Harrapa &amp; Moenjodaro,&nbsp;Gandhara&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Buddhist, Islamic &amp; Mughal Era to&nbsp;British Raj, all periods have imprints in this region. The<span> <strong>Indus valley civilization</strong></span> has still shrouded in mystery as their language has not yet been deciphered.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n',1,163,'agent','2024-03-14 21:42:13','2024-03-18 04:32:11'),(1413,12,'Buddhism & Gandhara','Buddhism & Gandhara','pakistantours/buddhism-gandhara','pakistantours/buddhism-gandhara','Buddhism & Gandhara',NULL,NULL,'Domestic Tour','USD','0',20,'','<p>&nbsp;</p>  <h4><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Price Includes:</strong></span></h4>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <ol style=\"list-style: decimal; padding-left: 20px;\"> 	<li>Private air conditioned transport</li> 	<li>Accommodation in standard hotels&nbsp;</li> 	