/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(2, 160, 234); font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Gurdwara Rori Sahib and Chaki Sahib:&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\n\n<p>Gurdwara Rori Sahib is 200 years old ancient temple and it is located in Eminabad.Gurdwara Rori Sahib, Gurdwara Chakki Sahib and Gurdwara Khuhi Bhai Laloimportant shrines of Sikhs are here.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n',0,163,'agent','2024-03-14 21:42:13','2024-03-18 04:39:00'),(1438,12,'Sarfaranga Jeep Ralley ','Sarfaranga Jeep Ralley ','pakistantours/jeep-safari','pakistantours/jeep-safari','Sarfaranga Jeep Ralley ',NULL,NULL,'Domestic Tour','USD','0',0,'','<h4><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What&rsquo;s Excluded:</span></h4>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\"> 	<li>Porters (for carrying personal equipment/luggage of participants)</li> 	<li>Extra expenses in change of tour plan due to the acts of nature/religious or political reasons.</li> 	<li>Entry Tickets, Lunch, Mineral Water, side orders, laundry services, telephone calls or any other service not mentioned above is to be charged separately.</li> </ul>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <h4><strong>Importance Note:</strong></h4>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\"> 	<li>In case of any change in tour plan, result in the change of cost and will be reflected in invoice accordingly. &frac34; hours +/- can be experienced during travelling in hilly areas due to any reason</li> 	<li>Hotels standard check in time 14:00hrs &amp; check out time 12:00hrs, late checkout will be extended till 14:00hrs, after that time 50% of the room rent will be charge till 18:00hrs, full night will be charged after 18:00hrs accordingly.</li> </ul>  <p><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(178, 34, 34);\">NOTE:</span>&nbsp;Above package is for minimum group of 10 persons</strong></p>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <h4><strong>Child Policy:</strong></h4>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\"> 	<li>Child below 07 years sharing parent&rsquo;s room is free (Max.02 children in a room)</li> 	<li>Child above 07yrs to 12&nbsp; years will be charged 50% of the adult cost</li> 	<li>Child above 12 treated as an adult</li> 	<li>The price does not include Breakfast &amp; Dinner for below 07yrs children</li> </ul>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <h4><strong>PAYMENT &amp; CANCELLATION POLICY:</strong></h4>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\"> 	<li>Reservations are made on first come first serve basis and confirmed on receipt of 50% advance payment.&nbsp;</li> 	<li>Cancellations not intimated at least 72 hours prior to departure are to be charged at the quoted rates.</li> 	<li>Remaining 50% payment to be cleared before departure.</li> </ul>  <p>&nbsp;</p>','<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Price excludes:</strong></span></h4>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style: decimal; padding-left: 20px;\">\n	<li>Late checkout, if different from standard checkout time</li>\n	<li>Personal insurance of clients/luggage</li>\n	<li>Refreshments</li>\n	<li>Zakh Competition(Rafting on traditional boats)</li>\n	<li>Laundry, beverages &amp; phone calls or other expenses of personal nature</li>\n	<li>Extra expenses due to the acts of nature and political reasons etc.</li>\n	<li>Medical aid, evacuation or extra expenses in emergencies</li>\n	<li>Any item not mentioned above</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>',NULL,0,0,'<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span>International event 3-day festival 23 to 25 August 19.<br />\nWith day trip to Deosai&mdash;on 25th August!&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span>Conquer the highest cold desert and create a legacy! 22 to 26 by Air&hellip;.</span></span></p>\n\n<p><br />\nIn the northern areas of Pakistan at an altitude of nearly 2,500 meters (8,202 feet). , the sand dunes located in Sarfaranga village are a wonderful creation of Allah, at Skardu, Gilgit-Baltistan in Pakistan. These sandbanks are also known as the cold desert with strong winds that shift the dunes, forming different shapes each time. This cold dessert is extended from Khaplu Valley to Nubra Ladakh and Shigar Skardu valley to Zanskar in India.<br />\nThis desert holds a unique place in the hearts of travelers due to its high altitude and cold region. The shooting stars and the moving galaxy spread in the sky in cold nights of Sarfaranga. The Indus River beside crystal clear water reflects the image of colorful trees, enhancing the beauty of Sarfaranga village.<br />\nDeosai&ndash;-The Last Sanctuary! The Deosai Plains are additionally home to the Red Fox, Golden Marmot, Himalayan Ibex, Gray Wolf, the Ladakh Urial, the Snow Leopard, and in excess of 124 inhabitant and transient flying creatures. Feathered creatures in the recreation center incorporate the Golden Eagle, Lammergeier, Griffon Vulture, Laggar Falcon, Peregrine Falcon, Kestrel, Sparrow hawk and Snow cock.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n',1,163,'agent','2024-03-14 21:42:13','2024-03-18 04:39:11'),(1439,12,'Kalash Festival Uchal','Kalash Festival Uchal ','pakistantours/kalash-festival-uchal','pakistantours/kalash-festival-uchal','Kalash Festival Uchal ',NULL,NULL,'Domestic Tour','USD','0',3,'','<p>&nbsp;</p>  <h4><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Includes:</strong></span></h4>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\"> 	<li>Accommodation&nbsp;</li> 	<li>Meals:</li> 	<li>04 Breakfast</li> 	<li>03 Lunch</li> 	<li>04 Dinner</li> 	<li>Luxury Air-conditioned Transport as per group size</li> 	<li>Fuel &amp; All Toll Taxes/Parking Fee</li> 	<li>Dedicated Driver</li> 	<li>4wd Jeeps for Off-Road Kalash Valley</li> 	<li>Entry Fee</li> 	<li>Tour Guide</li> </ul>  <p>&nbsp;</p>','<h4><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><strong>Not Incl...',NULL,0,0,'<p>Do experience the world unique culture of Kalash with Rehman Travels. It is better to see the culture once than hear about it a thousand times.</p>\n\n<p><br />\nUCHAL&nbsp; &ldquo;Thanksgiving movement&rdquo; in local language- is one of the famous religious festivals of the Kalash community celebrated by the Kalasha people every year on 20-22 August for the harvest and threshing of wheat crop in the three valleys of Bumburat, Birir and Rumbur.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><br />\nThe most remote and highly vulnerable community of Kalasha having unique traditions, values, customs is the happiest people of the world. None of the six key factors of happiness criteria applied in determining the international standard, but the Kalasha are known to be content and cheerful, as well as peaceful, showing gratitude and enjoying their simple pastoralist lives.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><br />\nKalash person&#39;s belief is that &ldquo;we have to live here in the heaven of Kalash and not in any other part of the world, so we are satisfied, we have enough resources to feed ourselves and our children. The Kalasha are never money oriented, we prefer peace and love that is everything to us. (Badsha Kalash)&hellip; we [the tribe] are famous for our faith in purity, we are pure souls like we don&rsquo;t do negative things, we are satisfied with our lives, in our traditions and give no harm to others, we believe that all living peacefully are pure souls&rdquo;. (Jia Kalasha).</p>\n\n<p><br />\nKalash celebrates every single event of life individually and collectively. Their social structured is established in a way which promote happiness, love, tolerance and respect to all living and non-living creature of God. The four landmark festivals are celebrated in May, August, September and December every year, providing space sand opportunities for other people to join them in these feasts.</p>\n\n<p><br />\nUchal festival provides an opportunity to the community to pay homage to nature by celebrating the harvest and also thanking their Creator for blessing them with good food and crops. They take a procession to a high plateau which is located outside of the village in Balangkuru and they pray to the Creator and this is where the long night of dancing begins.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><br />\nThe Kalashi people celebrate the pre-harvest with cheese, corn, and wine. The people of the Kalash valley love music and dance to the beat of drums. Women dance in a circle on different songs. An interesting fact about Kalashi people is that they do not mourn the deaths, rather they celebrate it as a movement of happy return of their soul to God. The best gift the Kalasha people expect from the friend is a big dance for the departed soul.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n',1,163,'agent','2024-03-14 21:42:13','2024-03-18 04:39:39'),(1440,12,'skardu tour packages | skardu travel packages | skardu trip','Book Skardu Tour and explore places in Skardu, kachura lake, kharpocho fort & deosai lake with rehmantravel.com with private accommodation & transportation','pakistantours/skardu-tour','pakistantours/skardu-tour','Skardu Tour ',NULL,NULL,'Domestic Tour','USD','0',0,'','<p>&nbsp;</p>  <h4><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><strong>Service Included:</strong></span></h4>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\"> 	<li>Accommodation</li> 	<li>Daily Breakfast</li> 	<li>4wd Vehicle for the whole trip</li> 	<li>Fuel&nbsp;</li> 	<li>Dedicated Driver</li> </ul>  <p>&nbsp;</p>','<h4><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><strong>Service Not Included:</strong></span></h4>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\">\n	<li>Porters (for carrying personal equipment/luggage of participant).</li>\n	<li>Extra expenses due to landslides\\road blocks.</li>\n	<li>Extra expenses due to the acts of nature/ religious and political reasons etc.</li>\n	<li>Lunch, Dinner, Mineral Water, side orders, Laundry service, telephone calls or any other service not mentioned above is to be charged separately.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><strong>Important Note:</strong></span></h4>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\">\n	<li>In case of any Change in tour plan, result in the change of cost and will be reflected in invoice accordingly. 3-4 hours can be experienced during traveling in hilly areas due to any reason.</li>\n	<li>Hotels Check-In time is 1400hrs &amp; Check out 1200hrs.</li>\n	<li>Late Check Out will be extended till 1400hrs, after that 50% of the room rate will be charged till 1800hrs.</li>\n	<li>Full night will be charged after 1800hrs accordingly.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><strong>Payment and Cancellation policy:</strong></span></h4>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\">\n	<li>Reservations are made on a first come first serve basis and confirmed on receipt of 50% advance payment.&nbsp;</li>\n	<li>Cancellations not intimated at least 72 hours prior to departure are to be charged at the quoted rates.</li>\n	<li>Remaining 50% payment to be cleared before departure.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><strong>Participants need to bring:</strong></span></h4>\n\n<ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\">\n	<li>Rain Coat</li>\n	<li>Sun Glasses</li>\n	<li>Warm Clothes</li>\n	<li>Joggers</li>\n	<li>Backpack</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>',NULL,0,0,'<p>Skardu is the land of mountain and the largest city of Gilgit-Baltistan. Snow-capped mountains, green meadows, waterfall, tall trees are the attractiveness of Skardu. It is famous for trekking and adventure spots. Skardu weather is calm and pleasant. Cultural festivals are celebrated in Skardu. People of Skardu are very hospitable and welcoming.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span><strong>Duration Of Tour:</strong></span></span></p>\n\n<ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style: square;\">\n	<li>&nbsp;5 Nights / 6 Days</li>\n</ul>\n',1,163,'agent','2024-03-14 21:42:13','2024-03-18 04:39:57'),(1441,12,'swat kalam tour | swat valley tour | kalam valley tour','Get the best swat kalam tour packages from rehmantravel.com. Beautiful places to visit, Swat valley, Kalam valley & Mingora with luxury tour services & guide','swat-kalam-tour','swat-kalam-tour','Swat Kalam Tour',NULL,NULL,'Domestic Tour','USD','0',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,0,'<p>Swat is also known as the Switzerland of Pakistan. Snow-capped peaks, waterfalls, magnificent lakes, lush green fields, pine forests attract tourists across the world. Swat is located in the Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province. Saidu Sharif is the capital of Swat and Mingora is the main town in Swat. Swat is very rich in culture and heritage. Carved wooden furniture is very famous and Swat cuisine is very toothsome.&nbsp;<br />\nKalam is an amazing small hill station in Swat. From Swat, you can easily reach to Kalam in 4 hours. Many marvelous lakes, stunning valleys are situated in Kalam. Kalam is the best place for trekking.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n',0,163,'agent','2024-03-14 21:42:13','2024-03-14 23:21:54'),(1442,12,'Hunza Valley | Naran Kaghan tour | kaghan valley| Hunza Tour','You will encounter a unique blend of entirely two different regions of Northern areas of Pakistan in this Tour Plan. One is “Naran Kaghan” of Khyber Phatunkhwa and the other is “Hunza” of Gilgit Baltistan. Both of the regions are blessed with countless amazing locations. The colors of Hunza and scen','pakistantours/naran-hunza-khunjrab-pass','pakistantours/naran-hunza-khunjrab-pass','Naran-Hunza-Khunjrab-Naltar',NULL,'fairy-medows.webp','Domestic Tour','PKR','40000',0,NULL,'<p>&nbsp;</p>  <h4><strong style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Price Includes:</strong></h4>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <ol> 	<li>Accommodation (Sharing Basis)</li> 	<li>&bull;<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Daily Breakfast &amp; Dinner (restricted with 01 Main Course)</li> 	<li>